<div id="abstract1" class="ltx_abstract"><h6 class="ltx_title ltx_title_abstract">Abstract</h6>
    
<p id="abstract1.1" class="ltx_p">Denoising Diffusion Probabilistic Models represent an entirely new class of generative AI methods that have yet to be fully explored. Critical damping has been successfully introduced in Critically-Damped Langevin Dynamics (CLD) and Critically-Damped Third-Order Langevin Dynamics (TOLD++), but has not yet been applied to dynamics of arbitrary order. The proposed line of work generalizes Higher-Order Langevin Dynamics (HOLD), a recent state-of-the-art diffusion method, by introducing the concept of critical damping from systems analysis.</p>
  
</div><span id="id2" class="ltx_note ltx_role_heading"><sup class="ltx_note_mark">†</sup><span class="ltx_note_outer"><span class="ltx_note_content"><sup class="ltx_note_mark">†</sup><span class="ltx_note_type">heading: </span>XX YYYY 1-<span class="ltx_ref ltx_missing_label ltx_ref_self"></span> MM/YY; Revised MM/YY MM/YY ??-????</span></span></span><span id="id3" class="ltx_note ltx_role_firstpage"><sup class="ltx_note_mark">†</sup><span class="ltx_note_outer"><span class="ltx_note_content"><sup class="ltx_note_mark">†</sup><span class="ltx_note_type">firstpage: </span>1</span></span></span>
<div class="ltx_classification"><h6 class="ltx_title ltx_title_classification">keywords</h6>
TOLD, CLD, DDPMs, Langevin Dynamics, Critical Damping

</div>
<section id="S1" class="ltx_section">
<h2 class="ltx_title ltx_title_section"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_section">1 </span>Introduction</h2>

<div id="S1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Fundamentally, generative AI converts a high-dimensional, and otherwise intractable, data distribution into a simple distribution. Today, the dominant methodology for image, video, and non-linguistic sample generation is the Denoising Diffusion Probabilistic Model (diffusion model) <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite"><a href="#bib.bib11" title="" class="ltx_ref">Sohl-Dickstein et al. (2015)</a>; <a href="#bib.bib6" title="" class="ltx_ref">Ho et al. (2020)</a></cite>. Our proposed enhancement to this framework accelerates convergence because modeling the <math id="S1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="n" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>n</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">n</annotation></semantics></math>th order diffusion-time derivative smooths the denoising process.</p>
</div>
<div id="S1.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S1.p2.1" class="ltx_p">NVIDIA’s seminal Critically-Damped Langevin Dynamics (CLD) improves upon the standard diffusion process by adding an auxiliary variable, referred to as velocity <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite"><a href="#bib.bib5" title="" class="ltx_ref">Dockhorn et al. (2022)</a></cite>. The addition of velocity smooths the data variable’s convergence from the data distribution to latent distribution, and vice versa, because the Ornstein-Uhlenbeck process is not directly applied to the data variable. The concept of “critical damping” is borrowed from classical systems theory to describe the family of optimal parameter choices. Third-Order Langevin Dynamics (TOLD) <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite"><a href="#bib.bib8" title="" class="ltx_ref">Shi and Liu (2024a)</a></cite> improves upon CLD by simplifying the forward and backward stochastic processes and adding a second auxiliary variable, acceleration. Critically-Damped Third-Order Langevin Dynamics (TOLD++) <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite"><a href="#bib.bib12" title="" class="ltx_ref">Sterling and Bugallo (2025)</a></cite> advances TOLD by deriving a set of critically-damped third-order dynamics and proving that these dynamics result in optimal convergence. Beyond optimality, critically damping the third-order system simplifies the TOLD algorithm, reducing computational cost. The invention of TOLD++ raises the question: is it possible to critically damp dynamics of arbitrary order? From our preliminary theoretical results, the answer is yes.</p>
</div>
<div id="S1.p3" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S1.p3.1" class="ltx_p">To push the potential of this technique even further, we propose Critically-Damped Higher-Order Langevin Dynamics (HOLD++). We further argue that critical damping is optimal, with a small caveat, and discuss the tradeoff between higher model orders and computational burden.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="S2" class="ltx_section">
<h2 class="ltx_title ltx_title_section"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_section">2 </span>Related Works</h2>

<div id="S2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Underdamped Diffusion Bridges <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite"><a href="#bib.bib1" title="" class="ltx_ref">Blessing et al. (2025)</a></cite> have recently been proposed to accelerate the dynamics of both the forward and backwards processes with control neural networks. Their approach fundamentally differs from this work’s as we only consider optimal constantly parameterized stochastic processes. It is important to note that in reference to the works of <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite"><a href="#bib.bib3" title="" class="ltx_ref">Cheng et al. (2017)</a>; <a href="#bib.bib1" title="" class="ltx_ref">Blessing et al. (2025)</a></cite>, that damping in this context is defined a bit differently: in these other works, Langevin dynamics without auxiliary variables are overdamped as they do not model system acceleration, and Langevin dynamics with one auxiliary variable are under damped.</p>
</div>
<div id="S2.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S2.p2.1" class="ltx_p">Since its invention, Higher Order Langevin Dynamics have found many applications, including the tasks of voice generation <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite"><a href="#bib.bib9" title="" class="ltx_ref">Shi and Liu (2024b)</a></cite> and noisy image restoration <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite"><a href="#bib.bib10" title="" class="ltx_ref">Shi and Liu (2024c)</a></cite>. They have even been adapted to operate on manifolds <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite"><a href="#bib.bib2" title="" class="ltx_ref">Bortoli et al. (2022)</a></cite>, and Lie Groups <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite"><a href="#bib.bib14" title="" class="ltx_ref">Zhu et al. (2025)</a></cite>. The latter has recently found application in generative modeling of chemical structures <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite"><a href="#bib.bib4" title="" class="ltx_ref">Cornet et al. (2025)</a></cite>.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="S3" class="ltx_section">
<h2 class="ltx_title ltx_title_section"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_section">3 </span>Methods</h2>

<div id="S3.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S3.p1.1" class="ltx_p">To define the order <math id="S3.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="n&gt;1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">n&gt;1</annotation></semantics></math> forward stochastic process <math id="S3.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p(\bm{x}_{t}|\bm{x}_{0},t)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝒙</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝒙</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p(\bm{x}_{t}|\bm{x}_{0},t)</annotation></semantics></math> with coefficients <math id="S3.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\gamma_{1},\gamma_{2},\ldots,\gamma_{n-1},\xi\in\mathbb{R}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>γ</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>γ</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>γ</mi><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>ξ</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi>ℝ</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\gamma_{1},\gamma_{2},\ldots,\gamma_{n-1},\xi\in\mathbb{R}</annotation></semantics></math>, we set</p>
<table id="S3.EGx1" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="S3.Ex1"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S3.Ex1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\bm{F}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>𝑭</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\bm{F}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S3.Ex1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\sum_{i=1}^{n-1}\gamma_{i}\left(\bm{E}_{i,i+1}-\bm{E}_{i+1,i}\right)-\xi\bm{E}_{n,n}," display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></munderover></mstyle><mrow><msub><mi>γ</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝑬</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mrow></msub><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>𝑬</mi><mrow><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo>,</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>ξ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>𝑬</mi><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow></msub></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\sum_{i=1}^{n-1}\gamma_{i}\left(\bm{E}_{i,i+1}-\bm{E}_{i+1,i}\right)-\xi\bm{E}_{n,n},</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S3.Ex1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\bm{G}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>𝑮</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\bm{G}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S3.Ex1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\sqrt{2\xi L^{-1}}\bm{E}_{n,n}," display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><msqrt><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>ξ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>L</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup></mrow></msqrt><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>𝑬</mi><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow></msub></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\sqrt{2\xi L^{-1}}\bm{E}_{n,n},</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S3.p1.2" class="ltx_p">where <math id="S3.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\bm{E}_{i,j}\in\mathbb{R}^{n\times n}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>𝑬</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub><mo>∈</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\bm{E}_{i,j}\in\mathbb{R}^{n\times n}</annotation></semantics></math> is the matrix of all zeros with a solitary one at index <math id="S3.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="i,j" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">i,j</annotation></semantics></math>.
For example, in the third order setting,</p>
<table id="S3.EGx2" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="S3.Ex2"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S3.Ex2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\bm{F}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>𝑭</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\bm{F}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S3.Ex2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\begin{bmatrix}0&amp;\gamma_{1}&amp;0\\
-\gamma_{1}&amp;0&amp;\gamma_{2}\\
0&amp;-\gamma_{2}&amp;-\xi\\
\end{bmatrix}," display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><mtable columnspacing="5pt" rowspacing="0pt"><mtr><mtd><mn>0</mn></mtd><mtd><msub><mi>γ</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></mtd><mtd><mn>0</mn></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd><mrow><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>γ</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></mrow></mtd><mtd><mn>0</mn></mtd><mtd><msub><mi>γ</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd><mn>0</mn></mtd><mtd><mrow><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>γ</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></mrow></mtd><mtd><mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>ξ</mi></mrow></mtd></mtr></mtable><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\begin{bmatrix}0&amp;\gamma_{1}&amp;0\\
-\gamma_{1}&amp;0&amp;\gamma_{2}\\
0&amp;-\gamma_{2}&amp;-\xi\\
\end{bmatrix},</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S3.Ex2.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\bm{G}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>𝑮</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\bm{G}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S3.Ex2.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\begin{bmatrix}0&amp;0&amp;0\\
0&amp;0&amp;0\\
0&amp;0&amp;\sqrt{2\xi L^{-1}}\\
\end{bmatrix}." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><mtable columnspacing="5pt" rowspacing="0pt"><mtr><mtd><mn>0</mn></mtd><mtd><mn>0</mn></mtd><mtd><mn>0</mn></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd><mn>0</mn></mtd><mtd><mn>0</mn></mtd><mtd><mn>0</mn></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd><mn>0</mn></mtd><mtd><mn>0</mn></mtd><mtd><msqrt><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>ξ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>L</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup></mrow></msqrt></mtd></mtr></mtable><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\begin{bmatrix}0&amp;0&amp;0\\
0&amp;0&amp;0\\
0&amp;0&amp;\sqrt{2\xi L^{-1}}\\
\end{bmatrix}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S3.p1.3" class="ltx_p">Then, the process evolves independently in <math id="S3.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="h" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>h</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">h</annotation></semantics></math> dimensions according to the stochastic differential equation (SDE)</p>
<table id="S3.E1" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S3.E1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="d\bm{x}_{t}=\mathcal{F}\bm{x}_{t}dt+\mathcal{G}d\bm{w}," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>𝒙</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℱ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>𝒙</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒢</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝒘</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">d\bm{x}_{t}=\mathcal{F}\bm{x}_{t}dt+\mathcal{G}d\bm{w},</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(1)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S3.p1.4" class="ltx_p">where <math id="S3.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{F}=\bm{F}\otimes\bm{I}_{h}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℱ</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>𝑭</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⊗</mo><msub><mi>𝑰</mi><mi>h</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{F}=\bm{F}\otimes\bm{I}_{h}</annotation></semantics></math>, and <math id="S3.p1.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{G}=\bm{G}\otimes\bm{I}_{h}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒢</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>𝑮</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⊗</mo><msub><mi>𝑰</mi><mi>h</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{G}=\bm{G}\otimes\bm{I}_{h}</annotation></semantics></math>. In Section <a href="#S5" title="5 Critical Damping ‣ Critically-Damped Higher-Order Langevin Dynamics" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">5</span></a>, we will derive how to choose <math id="S3.p1.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\gamma_{1},\gamma_{2},\ldots,\gamma_{n-1},\xi" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>γ</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>γ</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>γ</mi><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo>,</mo><mi>ξ</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\gamma_{1},\gamma_{2},\ldots,\gamma_{n-1},\xi</annotation></semantics></math> such that <math id="S3.p1.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\bm{F}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>𝑭</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\bm{F}</annotation></semantics></math> possesses only a single geometric eigenvalue.
The current problem of interest is to sample from the forward distribution governed by (<a href="#S3.E1" title="In 3 Methods ‣ Critically-Damped Higher-Order Langevin Dynamics" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">1</span></a>).
By construction, <math id="S3.p1.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p(\bm{x}_{t}|\bm{x}_{0},t)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝒙</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝒙</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p(\bm{x}_{t}|\bm{x}_{0},t)</annotation></semantics></math> is a Gaussian process, so the mean <math id="S3.p1.m12" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\bm{\mu}_{t}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>𝝁</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\bm{\mu}_{t}</annotation></semantics></math> and covariance <math id="S3.p1.m13" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\bm{\Sigma}_{t}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>𝚺</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\bm{\Sigma}_{t}</annotation></semantics></math> are governed by</p>
<table id="S3.EGx3" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="S3.E2"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S3.E2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\frac{d\bm{\mu}_{t}}{dt}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>𝝁</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></mrow><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\frac{d\bm{\mu}_{t}}{dt}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S3.E2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\mathcal{F}\bm{\mu}_{t}," display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℱ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>𝝁</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\mathcal{F}\bm{\mu}_{t},</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(2)</span></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="S3.E3"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S3.E3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\frac{d\bm{\Sigma}_{t}}{dt}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>𝚺</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></mrow><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\frac{d\bm{\Sigma}_{t}}{dt}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S3.E3.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\mathcal{F}\bm{\Sigma}_{t}+(\mathcal{F}\bm{\Sigma}_{t})^{T}+\mathcal{G}\mathcal{G}^{T}," display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℱ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>𝚺</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></mrow><mo>+</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℱ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>𝚺</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mi>T</mi></msup><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒢</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒢</mi><mi>T</mi></msup></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\mathcal{F}\bm{\Sigma}_{t}+(\mathcal{F}\bm{\Sigma}_{t})^{T}+\mathcal{G}\mathcal{G}^{T},</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(3)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S3.p1.5" class="ltx_p">as explained in <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite"><a href="#bib.bib13" title="" class="ltx_ref">Särkkä and Solin (2019)</a></cite>.
The first contribution of this paper is the simplification of the mean and covariance into completely analytical expressions, given by the following theorem.</p>
</div>
<div id="Thmtheorem1" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_theorem">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="Thmtheorem1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Theorem 1</span></span><span id="Thmtheorem1.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="Thmtheorem1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="Thmtheorem1.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="Thmtheorem1.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">The solutions to differential equations <a href="#S3.E2" title="In 3 Methods ‣ Critically-Damped Higher-Order Langevin Dynamics" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">2</span></a> and <a href="#S3.E3" title="In 3 Methods ‣ Critically-Damped Higher-Order Langevin Dynamics" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">3</span></a> are</span></p>
<table id="S3.EGx4" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="S3.E4"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S3.E4.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\bm{\mu}_{t}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>𝝁</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\bm{\mu}_{t}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S3.E4.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\exp(\mathcal{F}t)\bm{x}_{0}," display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>exp</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℱ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>𝒙</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\exp(\mathcal{F}t)\bm{x}_{0},</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(4)</span></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="S3.E5"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S3.E5.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\bm{\Sigma}_{t}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>𝚺</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\bm{\Sigma}_{t}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S3.E5.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=L^{-1}\bm{I}+\exp(\mathcal{F}t)\left(\bm{\Sigma}_{0}-L^{-1}\bm{I}\right)\exp(\mathcal{F}t)^{T}." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>L</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝑰</mi></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>exp</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℱ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝚺</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>−</mo><mrow><msup><mi>L</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝑰</mi></mrow></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>exp</mi><mo>⁡</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℱ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mi>T</mi></msup></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=L^{-1}\bm{I}+\exp(\mathcal{F}t)\left(\bm{\Sigma}_{0}-L^{-1}\bm{I}\right)\exp(\mathcal{F}t)^{T}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(5)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
</div>
<div id="S3.2" class="ltx_proof">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_font_italic ltx_title_proof">Proof.</h6>
<div id="S3.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S3.p2.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S3.p2.1.1" class="ltx_text">The expression for <math id="S3.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\bm{\mu}_{t}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>𝝁</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\bm{\mu}_{t}</annotation></semantics></math> is the canonical solution to multivariate linear differential equations. To evaluate the covariance differential equation, note that</span></p>
<table id="S3.EGx5" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="S3.Ex3"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S3.Ex3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\mathcal{G}\mathcal{G}^{T}=(2\xi L^{-1}\bm{E}_{n,n})\otimes\mathbf{I}_{h}=-L^{-1}\left(\mathcal{F}+\mathcal{F}^{T}\right)." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒢</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒢</mi><mi>T</mi></msup></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>ξ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>L</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>𝑬</mi><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><mo rspace="0.055em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo rspace="0.222em">⊗</mo><msub><mi>𝐈</mi><mi>h</mi></msub></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msup><mi>L</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℱ</mi><mo>+</mo><msup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℱ</mi><mi>T</mi></msup></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\mathcal{G}\mathcal{G}^{T}=(2\xi L^{-1}\bm{E}_{n,n})\otimes\mathbf{I}_{h}=-L^{-1}\left(\mathcal{F}+\mathcal{F}^{T}\right).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S3.p2.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="S3.p2.2.1" class="ltx_text">Then, the differential equation from Equation <a href="#S3.E3" title="In 3 Methods ‣ Critically-Damped Higher-Order Langevin Dynamics" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">3</span></a> is expressible as</span></p>
<table id="S3.EGx6" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="S3.Ex4"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S3.Ex4.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\frac{d}{dt}\left(\bm{\Sigma}_{t}-L^{-1}\mathbf{I}\right)=\mathcal{F}\left(\bm{\Sigma}_{t}-L^{-1}\mathbf{I}\right)+\left(\bm{\Sigma}_{t}-L^{-1}\mathbf{I}\right)\mathcal{F}^{T}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mi>d</mi><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝚺</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>−</mo><mrow><msup><mi>L</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝐈</mi></mrow></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℱ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝚺</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>−</mo><mrow><msup><mi>L</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝐈</mi></mrow></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝚺</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>−</mo><mrow><msup><mi>L</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝐈</mi></mrow></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℱ</mi><mi>T</mi></msup></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\frac{d}{dt}\left(\bm{\Sigma}_{t}-L^{-1}\mathbf{I}\right)=\mathcal{F}\left(\bm{\Sigma}_{t}-L^{-1}\mathbf{I}\right)+\left(\bm{\Sigma}_{t}-L^{-1}\mathbf{I}\right)\mathcal{F}^{T}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S3.p2.3" class="ltx_p"><span id="S3.p2.3.1" class="ltx_text">But, this is the continuous-time Lyapunov Equation with respect to the symmetric matrix <math id="S3.p2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(\bm{\Sigma}_{t}-L^{-1}\mathbf{I})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝚺</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>−</mo><mrow><msup><mi>L</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝐈</mi></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(\bm{\Sigma}_{t}-L^{-1}\mathbf{I})</annotation></semantics></math> that has solution</span></p>
<table id="S3.EGx7" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="S3.Ex5"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S3.Ex5.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\bm{\Sigma}_{t}-L^{-1}\bm{I}=\exp(\mathcal{F}t)\left(\bm{\Sigma}_{0}-L^{-1}\bm{I}\right)\exp(\mathcal{F}t)^{T}." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>𝚺</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>−</mo><mrow><msup><mi>L</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝑰</mi></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>exp</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℱ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝚺</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>−</mo><mrow><msup><mi>L</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝑰</mi></mrow></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>exp</mi><mo>⁡</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℱ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mi>T</mi></msup></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\bm{\Sigma}_{t}-L^{-1}\bm{I}=\exp(\mathcal{F}t)\left(\bm{\Sigma}_{0}-L^{-1}\bm{I}\right)\exp(\mathcal{F}t)^{T}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S3.p2.4" class="ltx_p"><span id="S3.p2.4.1" class="ltx_text">The result follows immediately.
∎</span></p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="S3.p3" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S3.p3.1" class="ltx_p">It is now trivial to evaluate the asymptotic distribution <math id="S3.p3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\lim_{t\to\infty}p_{t}(\bm{x})=p_{\infty}(\bm{x})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mo>lim</mo><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></mrow></msub><mrow><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝒙</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>p</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝒙</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\lim_{t\to\infty}p_{t}(\bm{x})=p_{\infty}(\bm{x})</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div>
<div id="Thmtheorem2" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_lemma">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="Thmtheorem2.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Lemma 2</span></span><span id="Thmtheorem2.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="Thmtheorem2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="Thmtheorem2.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="Thmtheorem2.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">If <math id="Thmtheorem2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\bm{F}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>𝐅</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\bm{F}</annotation></semantics></math> is negative definite, then <math id="Thmtheorem2.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\lim_{t\to\infty}\bm{\mu}_{t}=\bm{0}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mo>lim</mo><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></mrow></msub><msub><mi>𝛍</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>𝟎</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\lim_{t\to\infty}\bm{\mu}_{t}=\bm{0}</annotation></semantics></math>, and <math id="Thmtheorem2.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\lim_{t\to\infty}\bm{\Sigma}_{t}=L^{-1}\bm{I}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mo>lim</mo><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></mrow></msub><msub><mi>𝚺</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><msup><mi>L</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝐈</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\lim_{t\to\infty}\bm{\Sigma}_{t}=L^{-1}\bm{I}</annotation></semantics></math>; implying the following convergence in distribution <math id="Thmtheorem2.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p_{\infty}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>p</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p_{\infty}</annotation></semantics></math>:</span></p>
<table id="S3.EGx8" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="S3.Ex6"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S3.Ex6.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\mathbf{x}_{t}\xrightarrow{d}\mathcal{N}(\bm{0},L^{-1}\bm{I})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>𝐱</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mover accent="true"><mo>→</mo><mo mathsize="0.700em">𝑑</mo></mover><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒩</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>𝟎</mn><mo>,</mo><mrow><msup><mi>L</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝑰</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\mathbf{x}_{t}\xrightarrow{d}\mathcal{N}(\bm{0},L^{-1}\bm{I})</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
</div>
<div id="S3.3" class="ltx_proof">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_font_italic ltx_title_proof">Proof.</h6>
<div id="S3.p4" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S3.p4.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S3.p4.1.1" class="ltx_text">Since <math id="S3.p4.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\bm{F}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>𝑭</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\bm{F}</annotation></semantics></math> is negative definite, <math id="S3.p4.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\lim_{t\to\infty}\exp(\bm{F}t)=\bm{0}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mo>lim</mo><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></mrow></msub><mrow><mi>exp</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>𝑭</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>𝟎</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\lim_{t\to\infty}\exp(\bm{F}t)=\bm{0}</annotation></semantics></math>.
By Theorem <a href="#Thmtheorem1" title="Theorem 1. ‣ 3 Methods ‣ Critically-Damped Higher-Order Langevin Dynamics" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">1</span></a>, this implies</span></p>
<table id="S3.EGx9" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="S3.Ex7"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S3.Ex7.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\lim_{t\to\infty}\bm{\mu}_{t}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><munder><mo movablelimits="false">lim</mo><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></mrow></munder><msub><mi>𝝁</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\lim_{t\to\infty}\bm{\mu}_{t}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S3.Ex7.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\lim_{t\to\infty}\left(\exp(\bm{F}t)\otimes\bm{I}_{h}\right)\bm{x}_{0}=\bm{0}," display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo rspace="0.1389em">=</mo><mrow><munder><mo lspace="0.1389em" movablelimits="false" rspace="0em">lim</mo><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></mrow></munder><mrow><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>exp</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>𝑭</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow><mo rspace="0.055em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.222em">⊗</mo><msub><mi>𝑰</mi><mi>h</mi></msub></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>𝒙</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>𝟎</mn></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\lim_{t\to\infty}\left(\exp(\bm{F}t)\otimes\bm{I}_{h}\right)\bm{x}_{0}=\bm{0},</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="S3.Ex8"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S3.Ex8.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\lim_{t\to\infty}\bm{\Sigma}_{t}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><munder><mo movablelimits="false">lim</mo><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></mrow></munder><msub><mi>𝚺</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\lim_{t\to\infty}\bm{\Sigma}_{t}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S3.Ex8.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\lim_{t\to\infty}\left(L^{-1}\bm{I}+\exp(\bm{F}t)\left(\Sigma_{0}-L^{-1}\bm{I}\right)\exp(\bm{F}t)^{T}\right)\otimes\bm{I}_{h}=L^{-1}\bm{I}." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo rspace="0.1389em">=</mo><mrow><mrow><munder><mo lspace="0.1389em" movablelimits="false" rspace="0em">lim</mo><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></mrow></munder><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>L</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝑰</mi></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>exp</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>𝑭</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Σ</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>−</mo><mrow><msup><mi>L</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝑰</mi></mrow></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>exp</mi><mo>⁡</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>𝑭</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mi>T</mi></msup></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.055em">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.222em">⊗</mo><msub><mi>𝑰</mi><mi>h</mi></msub></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><msup><mi>L</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝑰</mi></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\lim_{t\to\infty}\left(L^{-1}\bm{I}+\exp(\bm{F}t)\left(\Sigma_{0}-L^{-1}\bm{I}\right)\exp(\bm{F}t)^{T}\right)\otimes\bm{I}_{h}=L^{-1}\bm{I}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S3.p4.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="S3.p4.2.1" class="ltx_text">∎</span></p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="S3.p5" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S3.p5.1" class="ltx_p">Lemma <a href="#Thmtheorem2" title="Lemma 2. ‣ 3 Methods ‣ Critically-Damped Higher-Order Langevin Dynamics" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">2</span></a> is simple yet consequential, upon executing the reverse process, one must start by sampling the asymptotic distribution <math id="S3.p5.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{N}(\bm{0},L^{-1}\bm{I})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒩</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>𝟎</mn><mo>,</mo><mrow><msup><mi>L</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝑰</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{N}(\bm{0},L^{-1}\bm{I})</annotation></semantics></math>. The computations in the Theorem <a href="#Thmtheorem1" title="Theorem 1. ‣ 3 Methods ‣ Critically-Damped Higher-Order Langevin Dynamics" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">1</span></a> rely on <math id="S3.p5.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\exp(\mathcal{F}t)=\exp(\bm{F}t)\otimes\bm{I}_{h}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>exp</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℱ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>exp</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>𝑭</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow><mo rspace="0.055em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.222em">⊗</mo><msub><mi>𝑰</mi><mi>h</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\exp(\mathcal{F}t)=\exp(\bm{F}t)\otimes\bm{I}_{h}</annotation></semantics></math>, which in this case of a single geometric eigenvalue, may be calculated as</p>
</div>
<div id="S3.p6" class="ltx_para">
<table id="S3.E6" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S3.E6.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\exp(\bm{F}t)=\exp(\lambda_{*}t)\sum_{k=0}^{n-1}\frac{(\bm{F}-\lambda_{*}\bm{I})^{k}t^{k}}{k!}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>exp</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>𝑭</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>exp</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>λ</mi><mo>∗</mo></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></munderover><mfrac><mrow><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>𝑭</mi><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mi>λ</mi><mo>∗</mo></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝑰</mi></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mi>k</mi></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>t</mi><mi>k</mi></msup></mrow><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>!</mo></mrow></mfrac></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\exp(\bm{F}t)=\exp(\lambda_{*}t)\sum_{k=0}^{n-1}\frac{(\bm{F}-\lambda_{*}\bm{I})^{k}t^{k}}{k!}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(6)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="S3.p7" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S3.p7.1" class="ltx_p">Originally when the system was not critically damped as in HOLD, Putzer’s spectral formula was used to calculate the matrix exponential <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite"><a href="#bib.bib7" title="" class="ltx_ref">Putzer (1966)</a></cite>. Critical Damping provides an analytically and computationally simpler procedure. The HOLD and HOLD++ algorithms are given in Algorithm <a href="#alg1" title="Algorithm 1 ‣ 3 Methods ‣ Critically-Damped Higher-Order Langevin Dynamics" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">1</span></a>. These methods are functionally equivalent, differing only by how <math id="S3.p7.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\exp(\bm{F}t)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>exp</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>𝑭</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\exp(\bm{F}t)</annotation></semantics></math> is calculated. Of note, for each incrementation of the order, memory cost increases only by <math id="S3.p7.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{O}(h)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒪</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>h</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{O}(h)</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div>
<figure id="alg1" class="ltx_float ltx_float_algorithm ltx_framed ltx_framed_top">
<figcaption class="ltx_caption"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_float"><span id="alg1.5" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Algorithm 1</span> </span>  <span id="alg1.6" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#FF0000;">HOLD</span>/<span id="alg1.7" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#0000FF;">HOLD++</span> Training Algorithm</figcaption>
<div id="alg1.8" class="ltx_listing ltx_framed ltx_framed_topbottom ltx_listing">
<div id="alg1.l1" class="ltx_listingline">
            <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline"><span id="alg1.l1.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;">1:</span></span>
            
            
          <span id="alg1.l1.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Input:</span> Data <math id="alg1.l1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\bm{q}_{0}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>𝒒</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\bm{q}_{0}</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="alg1.l1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Sigma_{0}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Σ</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Sigma_{0}</annotation></semantics></math>, and Score Network <math id="alg1.l1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathfrak{S}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>𝔖</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathfrak{S}</annotation></semantics></math>.

</div>
<div id="alg1.l2" class="ltx_listingline">
            <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline"><span id="alg1.l2.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;">2:</span></span>
            
            
          <span id="alg1.l2.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">for</span> <math id="alg1.l2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="k=1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">k=1</annotation></semantics></math> to <math id="alg1.l2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="n_{train}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>n</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>r</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>a</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">n_{train}</annotation></semantics></math> <span id="alg1.l2.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">do</span>

</div>
<div id="alg1.l3" class="ltx_listingline">
            <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline"><span id="alg1.l3.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;">3:</span></span>
            
            
            <math id="alg1.l3.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\bm{x}_{0}[0:d]\leftarrow\bm{q}_{0}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>𝒙</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mn>0</mn><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mi>d</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">←</mo><msub><mi>𝒒</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\bm{x}_{0}[0:d]\leftarrow\bm{q}_{0}</annotation></semantics></math>

</div>
<div id="alg1.l4" class="ltx_listingline">
            <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline"><span id="alg1.l4.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;">4:</span></span>
            
            
            <math id="alg1.l4.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\bm{x}_{0}[d:nd]\leftarrow\mathcal{N}(\bm{0},\frac{\alpha}{L}\bm{I})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>𝒙</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mi>n</mi><mi>d</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">←</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒩</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>𝟎</mn><mo>,</mo><mfrac><mi>α</mi><mi>L</mi></mfrac><mi>𝑰</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\bm{x}_{0}[d:nd]\leftarrow\mathcal{N}(\bm{0},\frac{\alpha}{L}\bm{I})</annotation></semantics></math>

</div>
<div id="alg1.l5" class="ltx_listingline">
            <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline"><span id="alg1.l5.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;">5:</span></span>
            
            
            <math id="alg1.l5.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="t\leftarrow\mathcal{U}(0,T)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">←</mo><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒰</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mi>T</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">t\leftarrow\mathcal{U}(0,T)</annotation></semantics></math>

</div>
<div id="alg1.l6" class="ltx_listingline">
            <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline"><span id="alg1.l6.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;">6:</span></span>
            
            
            Calculate <math id="alg1.l6.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\exp(\mathcal{F}t)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>exp</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℱ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\exp(\mathcal{F}t)</annotation></semantics></math> <span id="alg1.l6.3" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#FF0000;">using Putzer’s formula</span> <span id="alg1.l6.4" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#0000FF;">using (<a href="#S3.E6" title="In 3 Methods ‣ Critically-Damped Higher-Order Langevin Dynamics" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">6</span></a>)</span>

</div>
<div id="alg1.l7" class="ltx_listingline">
            <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline"><span id="alg1.l7.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;">7:</span></span>
            
            
            Calculate <math id="alg1.l7.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\bm{\mu}_{t},\bm{\Sigma}_{t}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>𝝁</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>𝚺</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\bm{\mu}_{t},\bm{\Sigma}_{t}</annotation></semantics></math> using Theorem <a href="#Thmtheorem1" title="Theorem 1. ‣ 3 Methods ‣ Critically-Damped Higher-Order Langevin Dynamics" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">1</span></a>, <span id="alg1.l7.3" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#0000FF;">discovered in this manuscript</span>.

</div>
<div id="alg1.l8" class="ltx_listingline">
            <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline"><span id="alg1.l8.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;">8:</span></span>
            
            
            Take <math id="alg1.l8.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\bm{L}_{t}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>𝑳</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\bm{L}_{t}</annotation></semantics></math>, the Cholesky Decomposition of <math id="alg1.l8.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\bm{\Sigma}_{t}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>𝚺</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\bm{\Sigma}_{t}</annotation></semantics></math>

</div>
<div id="alg1.l9" class="ltx_listingline">
            <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline"><span id="alg1.l9.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;">9:</span></span>
            
            
            <math id="alg1.l9.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\bm{\epsilon_{1}},\bm{\epsilon_{2}},\ldots,\bm{\epsilon_{n}}\sim\mathcal{N}(\bm{0},\bm{I}_{h})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_mathvariant_bold-italic" mathvariant="bold-italic">ϵ</mi><mn>𝟏</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_mathvariant_bold-italic" mathvariant="bold-italic">ϵ</mi><mn>𝟐</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_mathvariant_bold-italic" mathvariant="bold-italic">ϵ</mi><mi>𝒏</mi></msub><mo>∼</mo><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒩</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>𝟎</mn><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>𝑰</mi><mi>h</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\bm{\epsilon_{1}},\bm{\epsilon_{2}},\ldots,\bm{\epsilon_{n}}\sim\mathcal{N}(\bm{0},\bm{I}_{h})</annotation></semantics></math>

</div>
<div id="alg1.l10" class="ltx_listingline">
            <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline"><span id="alg1.l10.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;">10:</span></span>
            
            
            <math id="alg1.l10.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\bm{\epsilon}_{full}\leftarrow\begin{pmatrix}\bm{\epsilon_{1}}^{T}&amp;\bm{\epsilon_{2}}^{T}&amp;\ldots&amp;\bm{\epsilon_{n}}^{T}\\
\end{pmatrix}^{T}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_mathvariant_bold-italic" mathvariant="bold-italic">ϵ</mi><mrow><mi>f</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>u</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>l</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>l</mi></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">←</mo><msup><mrow><mo>(</mo><mtable columnspacing="5pt"><mtr><mtd><mmultiscripts><mi class="ltx_mathvariant_bold-italic" mathvariant="bold-italic">ϵ</mi><mn>𝟏</mn><mrow></mrow><mrow></mrow><mi>T</mi></mmultiscripts></mtd><mtd><mmultiscripts><mi class="ltx_mathvariant_bold-italic" mathvariant="bold-italic">ϵ</mi><mn>𝟐</mn><mrow></mrow><mrow></mrow><mi>T</mi></mmultiscripts></mtd><mtd><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi></mtd><mtd><mmultiscripts><mi class="ltx_mathvariant_bold-italic" mathvariant="bold-italic">ϵ</mi><mi>𝒏</mi><mrow></mrow><mrow></mrow><mi>T</mi></mmultiscripts></mtd></mtr></mtable><mo>)</mo></mrow><mi>T</mi></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\bm{\epsilon}_{full}\leftarrow\begin{pmatrix}\bm{\epsilon_{1}}^{T}&amp;\bm{\epsilon_{2}}^{T}&amp;\ldots&amp;\bm{\epsilon_{n}}^{T}\\
\end{pmatrix}^{T}</annotation></semantics></math>

</div>
<div id="alg1.l11" class="ltx_listingline">
            <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline"><span id="alg1.l11.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;">11:</span></span>
            
            
            <math id="alg1.l11.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\bm{x}_{t}\leftarrow\bm{\mu}_{t}+\bm{L}_{t}\bm{\epsilon}_{full}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>𝒙</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">←</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝝁</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>+</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝑳</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_mathvariant_bold-italic" mathvariant="bold-italic">ϵ</mi><mrow><mi>f</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>u</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>l</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>l</mi></mrow></msub></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\bm{x}_{t}\leftarrow\bm{\mu}_{t}+\bm{L}_{t}\bm{\epsilon}_{full}</annotation></semantics></math>

</div>
<div id="alg1.l12" class="ltx_listingline">
            <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline"><span id="alg1.l12.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;">12:</span></span>
            
            
            <math id="alg1.l12.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="l_{t}\leftarrow\left(\bm{L}_{t}[nd,nd]\right)^{-1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>l</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">←</mo><msup><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝑳</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>d</mi></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>d</mi></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">l_{t}\leftarrow\left(\bm{L}_{t}[nd,nd]\right)^{-1}</annotation></semantics></math> <span id="alg1.l12.3" class="ltx_text" style="float:right;"><math id="alg1.l12.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\triangleright" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mo>⊳</mo><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\triangleright</annotation></semantics></math> Take scalar inverse of Cholesky matrix element
</span>
</div>
<div id="alg1.l13" class="ltx_listingline">
            <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline"><span id="alg1.l13.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;">13:</span></span>
            
            
            <math id="alg1.l13.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\bm{s}_{\theta}\leftarrow\mathfrak{S}(\bm{x}_{t},t)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>𝒔</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">←</mo><mrow><mi>𝔖</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝒙</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\bm{s}_{\theta}\leftarrow\mathfrak{S}(\bm{x}_{t},t)</annotation></semantics></math> <span id="alg1.l13.3" class="ltx_text" style="float:right;"><math id="alg1.l13.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\triangleright" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mo>⊳</mo><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\triangleright</annotation></semantics></math> <math id="alg1.l13.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\theta" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>θ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\theta</annotation></semantics></math> are score network parameters
</span>
</div>
<div id="alg1.l14" class="ltx_listingline">
            <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline"><span id="alg1.l14.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;">14:</span></span>
            
            
            <math id="alg1.l14.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{L}\leftarrow||\bm{\epsilon}_{n}+\frac{\bm{s}_{\theta}}{l_{t}}||^{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><mo stretchy="false">←</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_mathvariant_bold-italic" mathvariant="bold-italic">ϵ</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo>+</mo><mfrac><msub><mi>𝒔</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub><msub><mi>l</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></mfrac></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{L}\leftarrow||\bm{\epsilon}_{n}+\frac{\bm{s}_{\theta}}{l_{t}}||^{2}</annotation></semantics></math>

</div>
<div id="alg1.l15" class="ltx_listingline">
            <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline"><span id="alg1.l15.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;">15:</span></span>
            
            
            <span id="alg1.l15.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Backpropagate</span> through <math id="alg1.l15.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{L}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{L}</annotation></semantics></math>

</div>
<div id="alg1.l16" class="ltx_listingline">
            <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline"><span id="alg1.l16.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;">16:</span></span>
            
            
          <span id="alg1.l16.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">end</span> <span id="alg1.l16.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">for</span>
</div>
</div>
</figure>
<div id="S3.p8" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S3.p8.1" class="ltx_p">A consequential result is proven in Theorem <a href="#S4.Ex9" title="Theorem 3. ‣ 4 Optimality of Critical Damping ‣ Critically-Damped Higher-Order Langevin Dynamics" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">3</span></a>, that the critically damped parameter choice is optimal for a fixed trace of the forward matrix <math id="S3.p8.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{F}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>𝐅</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{F}</annotation></semantics></math>. This result generalizes the optimality known for second-order dynamics and proven for third-order dynamics in <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite"><a href="#bib.bib12" title="" class="ltx_ref">Sterling and Bugallo (2025)</a></cite>. There is a small caveat discussed after the theorem, but this result holds on unconstrained <math id="S3.p8.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\gamma_{1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>γ</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\gamma_{1}</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="S4" class="ltx_section">
<h2 class="ltx_title ltx_title_section"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_section">4 </span>Optimality of Critical Damping</h2>

<div id="Thmtheorem3" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_theorem">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="Thmtheorem3.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Theorem 3</span></span><span id="Thmtheorem3.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="Thmtheorem3.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="Thmtheorem3.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="Thmtheorem3.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">If <math id="Thmtheorem3.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\xi" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>ξ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\xi</annotation></semantics></math> is fixed, then the critically damped parameter choices are optimal according to the following objective:</span></p>
<table id="S4.Ex9" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S4.Ex9.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\min_{\gamma_{1},\gamma_{2},\gamma_{3},\ldots,\gamma_{n-1}}\max\bigg(\operatorname{Re}\left(\operatorname{eig}(\mathbf{F})\right)\bigg)." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><munder><mi>min</mi><mrow><msub><mi>γ</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>γ</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>γ</mi><mn>3</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>γ</mi><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub></mrow></munder><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mrow><mi>max</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="2.100em" minsize="2.100em">(</mo><mrow><mi>Re</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mi>eig</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝐅</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="2.100em" minsize="2.100em">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\min_{\gamma_{1},\gamma_{2},\gamma_{3},\ldots,\gamma_{n-1}}\max\bigg(\operatorname{Re}\left(\operatorname{eig}(\mathbf{F})\right)\bigg).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
</div>
<div id="S4.2" class="ltx_proof">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_font_italic ltx_title_proof">Proof.</h6>
<div id="S4.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S4.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S4.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text">Recall the following identity for matrix trace in terms of the eigenvalues <math id="S4.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\lambda_{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>λ</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\lambda_{i}</annotation></semantics></math> of <math id="S4.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{F}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>𝐅</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{F}</annotation></semantics></math>:</span></p>
</div>
<div id="S4.p2" class="ltx_para">
<table id="S4.Ex10" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S4.Ex10.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="Tr(\mathbf{F})=\sum_{i=1}^{n}\lambda_{i}=-\xi\quad\quad\to\quad\quad\xi=-\sum_{i=1}^{n}\lambda_{i}" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>T</mi><mi>r</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝐅</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo rspace="0.111em">=</mo><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>n</mi></munderover><msub><mi>λ</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo rspace="0em">=</mo><mo lspace="0em">−</mo><mi>ξ</mi><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mi>ξ</mi><mo rspace="0em">=</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.055em">−</mo><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>n</mi></munderover><msub><mi>λ</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">Tr(\mathbf{F})=\sum_{i=1}^{n}\lambda_{i}=-\xi\quad\quad\to\quad\quad\xi=-\sum_{i=1}^{n}\lambda_{i}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="S4.p3" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S4.p3.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S4.p3.1.1" class="ltx_text">Consider only the real parts of each eigenvalue, as complex eigenvalues must come in conjugate pairs and cancel out as <math id="S4.p3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\xi" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>ξ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\xi</annotation></semantics></math> is real valued. Optimality under <math id="S4.p3.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\operatorname{min}_{\gamma_{1},\gamma_{2},\ldots,\gamma_{n-1}}\operatorname{\max}_{i}\lambda_{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>min</mi><mrow><msub><mi>γ</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>γ</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>γ</mi><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><msub><mi>max</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>λ</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\operatorname{min}_{\gamma_{1},\gamma_{2},\ldots,\gamma_{n-1}}\operatorname{\max}_{i}\lambda_{i}</annotation></semantics></math> occurs when <math id="S4.p3.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\lambda_{1}=\lambda_{2}=\ldots=\lambda_{n}=-\frac{\xi}{n}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>λ</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>λ</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>=</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>λ</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo>−</mo><mfrac><mi>ξ</mi><mi>n</mi></mfrac></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\lambda_{1}=\lambda_{2}=\ldots=\lambda_{n}=-\frac{\xi}{n}</annotation></semantics></math>; if any eigenvalue is less than <math id="S4.p3.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="-\frac{\xi}{n}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>−</mo><mfrac><mi>ξ</mi><mi>n</mi></mfrac></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">-\frac{\xi}{n}</annotation></semantics></math>, then at least one other must be greater to conserve the sum, resulting in a suboptimal objective.</span></p>
</div>
<div id="S4.p4" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S4.p4.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S4.p4.1.1" class="ltx_text">∎</span></p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="S4.p5" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S4.p5.1" class="ltx_p">It is important to note that the previous proof does not assume <math id="S4.p5.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\gamma_{1}=1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>γ</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\gamma_{1}=1</annotation></semantics></math> and therefore is not the same as being optimal under the objective <math id="S4.p5.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\min_{\gamma_{2},\gamma_{3},\ldots,\gamma_{n-1},\xi}\max\bigg(\operatorname{Re}\left(\operatorname{eig}(\mathbf{F})\right)\bigg)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>min</mi><mrow><msub><mi>γ</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>γ</mi><mn>3</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>γ</mi><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo>,</mo><mi>ξ</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mrow><mi>max</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="2.100em" minsize="2.100em">(</mo><mrow><mi>Re</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mi>eig</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝐅</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="2.100em" minsize="2.100em">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\min_{\gamma_{2},\gamma_{3},\ldots,\gamma_{n-1},\xi}\max\bigg(\operatorname{Re}\left(\operatorname{eig}(\mathbf{F})\right)\bigg)</annotation></semantics></math>. However, the <math id="S4.p5.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{F}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>𝐅</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{F}</annotation></semantics></math> matrix generated according to the objectives <math id="S4.p5.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\min_{\gamma_{2},\gamma_{3},\ldots,\gamma_{n-1},\xi}\max\bigg(\operatorname{Re}\left(\operatorname{eig}(\mathbf{F})\right)\bigg)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>min</mi><mrow><msub><mi>γ</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>γ</mi><mn>3</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>γ</mi><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo>,</mo><mi>ξ</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mrow><mi>max</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="2.100em" minsize="2.100em">(</mo><mrow><mi>Re</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mi>eig</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝐅</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="2.100em" minsize="2.100em">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\min_{\gamma_{2},\gamma_{3},\ldots,\gamma_{n-1},\xi}\max\bigg(\operatorname{Re}\left(\operatorname{eig}(\mathbf{F})\right)\bigg)</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="S4.p5.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\min_{\gamma_{1},\gamma_{2},\ldots,\gamma_{n-1}}\max\bigg(\operatorname{Re}\left(\operatorname{eig}(\mathbf{F})\right)\bigg)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>min</mi><mrow><msub><mi>γ</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>γ</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>γ</mi><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mrow><mi>max</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="2.100em" minsize="2.100em">(</mo><mrow><mi>Re</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mi>eig</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝐅</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="2.100em" minsize="2.100em">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\min_{\gamma_{1},\gamma_{2},\ldots,\gamma_{n-1}}\max\bigg(\operatorname{Re}\left(\operatorname{eig}(\mathbf{F})\right)\bigg)</annotation></semantics></math>, only differ by a scaling factor. This means that the behavior of the algorithm remains exactly the same, with just a slightly different signal to noise ratio (SNR). <math id="S4.p5.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\gamma_{1}=1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>γ</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\gamma_{1}=1</annotation></semantics></math> is a more convenient design choice as it is easier to fix this than some arbitrary value of <math id="S4.p5.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\xi" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>ξ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\xi</annotation></semantics></math>, therefore it is fixed instead of <math id="S4.p5.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\xi" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>ξ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\xi</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="S5" class="ltx_section">
<h2 class="ltx_title ltx_title_section"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_section">5 </span>Critical Damping</h2>

<div id="Thmtheorem4" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_theorem">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="Thmtheorem4.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Theorem 4</span></span><span id="Thmtheorem4.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="Thmtheorem4.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="Thmtheorem4.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="Thmtheorem4.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">For <math id="Thmtheorem4.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="n&gt;1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">n&gt;1</annotation></semantics></math>, define
<math id="Thmtheorem4.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\bm{F}=\sum_{i=1}^{n-1}\gamma_{i}\left(\bm{E}_{i,i+1}-\bm{E}_{i+1,i}\right)-\xi\bm{E}_{n,n}," display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>𝐅</mi><mo rspace="0.111em">=</mo><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mo>∑</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msubsup><mrow><msub><mi>γ</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝐄</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mrow></msub><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>𝐄</mi><mrow><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo>,</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>ξ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>𝐄</mi><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow></msub></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\bm{F}=\sum_{i=1}^{n-1}\gamma_{i}\left(\bm{E}_{i,i+1}-\bm{E}_{i+1,i}\right)-\xi\bm{E}_{n,n},</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="Thmtheorem4.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\bm{G}=\sqrt{2\xi L^{-1}}\bm{E}_{n,n}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>𝐆</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><msqrt><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>ξ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>L</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup></mrow></msqrt><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>𝐄</mi><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow></msub></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\bm{G}=\sqrt{2\xi L^{-1}}\bm{E}_{n,n}</annotation></semantics></math> for <math id="Thmtheorem4.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\bm{E}_{i,j}\in\mathbb{R}^{n\times n}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>𝐄</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub><mo>∈</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\bm{E}_{i,j}\in\mathbb{R}^{n\times n}</annotation></semantics></math>
the one-hot basis for the vector space of matrices, as in Section <a href="#S3" title="3 Methods ‣ Critically-Damped Higher-Order Langevin Dynamics" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">3</span></a>.
If</span></p>
<table id="S5.EGx10" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="S5.Ex11"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S5.Ex11.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\gamma_{n-i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>γ</mi><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\gamma_{n-i}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S5.Ex11.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=|\lambda_{*}|\sqrt{\frac{n^{2}-i^{2}}{4i^{2}-1}}," display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><msub><mi>λ</mi><mo>∗</mo></msub><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msqrt><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><msup><mi>n</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>−</mo><msup><mi>i</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><mrow><mrow><mn>4</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>i</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mfrac></mstyle></msqrt></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=|\lambda_{*}|\sqrt{\frac{n^{2}-i^{2}}{4i^{2}-1}},</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><span id="S5.Ex11.5.1" class="ltx_text ltx_markedasmath ltx_font_italic">and</span></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S5.Ex11.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\xi" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>ξ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\xi</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S5.Ex11.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=n|\lambda_{*}|," display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><msub><mi>λ</mi><mo>∗</mo></msub><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=n|\lambda_{*}|,</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="Thmtheorem4.p1.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="Thmtheorem4.p1.2.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">for <math id="Thmtheorem4.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="i\in\{1,2,\ldots,n-1\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>2</mn><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">i\in\{1,2,\ldots,n-1\}</annotation></semantics></math>, then <math id="Thmtheorem4.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\bm{F}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>𝐅</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\bm{F}</annotation></semantics></math> has a single geometric eigenvalue <math id="Thmtheorem4.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\lambda_{*}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>λ</mi><mo>∗</mo></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\lambda_{*}</annotation></semantics></math>; making <math id="Thmtheorem4.p1.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\bm{F}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>𝐅</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\bm{F}</annotation></semantics></math> critically damped.
By convention, <math id="Thmtheorem4.p1.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\gamma_{1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>γ</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\gamma_{1}</annotation></semantics></math> is set to <math id="Thmtheorem4.p1.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>1</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">1</annotation></semantics></math>, in this case <math id="Thmtheorem4.p1.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\lambda_{*}=-\sqrt{2n-3}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>λ</mi><mo>∗</mo></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo>−</mo><msqrt><mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>3</mn></mrow></msqrt></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\lambda_{*}=-\sqrt{2n-3}</annotation></semantics></math>.</span></p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="S5.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S5.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Note the abuse of notation while setting <math id="S5.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\gamma_{n-i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>γ</mi><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\gamma_{n-i}</annotation></semantics></math>. In the chosen notation, the <math id="S5.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="n" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>n</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">n</annotation></semantics></math> in the formula is implied by the <math id="S5.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="n" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>n</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">n</annotation></semantics></math> before the minus sign in the index.<span id="footnote1" class="ltx_note ltx_role_footnote"><sup class="ltx_note_mark">1</sup><span class="ltx_note_outer"><span class="ltx_note_content"><sup class="ltx_note_mark">1</sup>
            <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_note">1</span>
            
            
            
          For example, <math id="footnote1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\gamma_{n-2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>γ</mi><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\gamma_{n-2}</annotation></semantics></math> is the <math id="footnote1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(n-2)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(n-2)</annotation></semantics></math>th value in the model of order <math id="footnote1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="n" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>n</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">n</annotation></semantics></math> while <math id="footnote1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\gamma_{(n-1)-1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>γ</mi><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\gamma_{(n-1)-1}</annotation></semantics></math> is the <math id="footnote1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(n-2)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(n-2)</annotation></semantics></math>th value in the model of order <math id="footnote1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="n-1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">n-1</annotation></semantics></math>, and in general, <math id="footnote1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\gamma_{n-2}\neq\gamma_{(n-1)-1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>γ</mi><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msub><mo>≠</mo><msub><mi>γ</mi><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\gamma_{n-2}\neq\gamma_{(n-1)-1}</annotation></semantics></math>.</span></span></span>
Since <math id="S5.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="n" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>n</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">n</annotation></semantics></math> is fixed throughout the theory of this paper, we further refine the notation and understand <math id="S5.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\gamma_{i}=\gamma_{n-(n-i)}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>γ</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>γ</mi><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>−</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\gamma_{i}=\gamma_{n-(n-i)}</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div>
<section id="S5.SS1" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">5.1 </span>From Matrices to Polynomials</h3>

<div id="S5.SS1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S5.SS1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Establishing Theorem <a href="#Thmtheorem4" title="Theorem 4. ‣ 5 Critical Damping ‣ Critically-Damped Higher-Order Langevin Dynamics" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">4</span></a> requires several intermediate steps; the first is to express the characteristic polynomial of <math id="S5.SS1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\bm{F}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>𝑭</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\bm{F}</annotation></semantics></math>.
For <math id="S5.SS1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="j\in\{1,2,\ldots,n\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>2</mn><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">j\in\{1,2,\ldots,n\}</annotation></semantics></math>, define <math id="S5.SS1.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="d_{j}:\mathbb{R}\to\mathbb{R}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>d</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><mi>ℝ</mi><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mi>ℝ</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">d_{j}:\mathbb{R}\to\mathbb{R}</annotation></semantics></math> to be the characteristic polynomial of the submatrix containing the first <math id="S5.SS1.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="j" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>j</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">j</annotation></semantics></math> rows and first <math id="S5.SS1.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="j" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>j</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">j</annotation></semantics></math> columns of <math id="S5.SS1.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\bm{F}+\xi\bm{E}_{n,n}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>𝑭</mi><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>ξ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>𝑬</mi><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow></msub></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\bm{F}+\xi\bm{E}_{n,n}</annotation></semantics></math> in order.
We work out an expression for <math id="S5.SS1.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="d_{j}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>d</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">d_{j}</annotation></semantics></math> in Lemma <a href="#Thmtheorem5" title="Lemma 5. ‣ 5.2 From Polynomials to Their Coefficients ‣ 5 Critical Damping ‣ Critically-Damped Higher-Order Langevin Dynamics" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">5</span></a>.
For now, it is easy to verify that taking a partial Laplace expansion gives</p>
<table id="S5.EGx11" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="S5.E7"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S5.E7.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle d_{j+1}(\lambda)=-\lambda d_{j}(\lambda)+\gamma_{j}^{2}d_{j-1}(\lambda)." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>d</mi><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>λ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>λ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>d</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>λ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>γ</mi><mi>j</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>d</mi><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>λ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle d_{j+1}(\lambda)=-\lambda d_{j}(\lambda)+\gamma_{j}^{2}d_{j-1}(\lambda).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(7)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S5.SS1.p1.2" class="ltx_p">Finally, define <math id="S5.SS1.p1.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="q:\mathbb{R}\to\mathbb{R}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>q</mi><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><mi>ℝ</mi><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mi>ℝ</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">q:\mathbb{R}\to\mathbb{R}</annotation></semantics></math> to be the characteristic polynomial of <math id="S5.SS1.p1.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\bm{F}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>𝑭</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\bm{F}</annotation></semantics></math>.
Then,</p>
<table id="S5.EGx12" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="S5.Ex12"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S5.Ex12.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle q(\lambda)=\mathrm{char}\left[\bm{F}+\xi\bm{E}_{n,n}-\xi\bm{E}_{n,n}\right](\lambda)=d_{n}(\lambda)-\xi d_{n-1}(\lambda)," display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>q</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>λ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>char</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>𝑭</mi><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>ξ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>𝑬</mi><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow></msub></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>ξ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>𝑬</mi><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow></msub></mrow></mrow><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>λ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>d</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>λ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>ξ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>d</mi><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>λ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle q(\lambda)=\mathrm{char}\left[\bm{F}+\xi\bm{E}_{n,n}-\xi\bm{E}_{n,n}\right](\lambda)=d_{n}(\lambda)-\xi d_{n-1}(\lambda),</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S5.SS1.p1.3" class="ltx_p">due to the multilinearity of the determinant.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="S5.SS2" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">5.2 </span>From Polynomials to Their Coefficients</h3>

<div id="S5.SS2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S5.SS2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Now, to express <math id="S5.SS2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="q" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>q</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">q</annotation></semantics></math> as a closed form in <math id="S5.SS2.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\lambda" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>λ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\lambda</annotation></semantics></math>, we introduce the bivariate sequence</p>
<table id="S5.E8" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S5.E8.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="s_{j,k}=\begin{cases}\gamma_{j}^{2}s_{j-2,k-1}+s_{j-1,k},&amp;\text{for }j&gt;2k-2,\\
1,&amp;\text{for }k=0,\\
0,&amp;\text{otherwise}.\end{cases}" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>s</mi><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo>{</mo><mtable columnspacing="5pt" displaystyle="true" rowspacing="0pt"><mtr><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi>γ</mi><mi>j</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>s</mi><mrow><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mrow></msub></mrow><mo>+</mo><msub><mi>s</mi><mrow><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo>,</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow></mtd><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><mrow><mrow><mtext>for </mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow><mo>&gt;</mo><mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo></mrow></mtd><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><mrow><mrow><mtext>for </mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo></mrow></mtd><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><mtext>otherwise</mtext><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow></mtd></mtr></mtable></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">s_{j,k}=\begin{cases}\gamma_{j}^{2}s_{j-2,k-1}+s_{j-1,k},&amp;\text{for }j&gt;2k-2,\\
1,&amp;\text{for }k=0,\\
0,&amp;\text{otherwise}.\end{cases}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(8)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="S5.SS2.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S5.SS2.p2.1" class="ltx_p">Then, we have the following expression for <math id="S5.SS2.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="d_{j}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>d</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">d_{j}</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div>
<div id="Thmtheorem5" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_lemma">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="Thmtheorem5.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Lemma 5</span></span><span id="Thmtheorem5.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="Thmtheorem5.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="Thmtheorem5.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><math id="Thmtheorem5.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="d_{j}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>d</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">d_{j}</annotation></semantics></math><span id="Thmtheorem5.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic"> as defined in Definition <a href="#S5.E7" title="In 5.1 From Matrices to Polynomials ‣ 5 Critical Damping ‣ Critically-Damped Higher-Order Langevin Dynamics" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">7</span></a>, and <math id="Thmtheorem5.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="s_{j,k}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>s</mi><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">s_{j,k}</annotation></semantics></math> as defined in Equation <a href="#S5.E8" title="In 5.2 From Polynomials to Their Coefficients ‣ 5 Critical Damping ‣ Critically-Damped Higher-Order Langevin Dynamics" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">8</span></a> are related by</span></p>
<table id="S5.EGx13" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="S5.Ex13"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S5.Ex13.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle d_{j}(\lambda)=(-1)^{j}\sum_{k=0}^{\lfloor j/2\rfloor}\lambda^{j-2k}s_{j-1,k}." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>d</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>λ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mi>j</mi></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">⌊</mo><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>/</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">⌋</mo></mrow></munderover></mstyle><mrow><msup><mi>λ</mi><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>−</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>s</mi><mrow><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo>,</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow></msub></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle d_{j}(\lambda)=(-1)^{j}\sum_{k=0}^{\lfloor j/2\rfloor}\lambda^{j-2k}s_{j-1,k}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
</div>
<div id="S5.SS2.p3" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S5.SS2.p3.1" class="ltx_p">Lemma <a href="#Thmtheorem5" title="Lemma 5. ‣ 5.2 From Polynomials to Their Coefficients ‣ 5 Critical Damping ‣ Critically-Damped Higher-Order Langevin Dynamics" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">5</span></a> is proved in Appendix <a href="#A1" title="Appendix A Proof of Lemma ‣ Critically-Damped Higher-Order Langevin Dynamics" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">A</span></a>. Immediately, Lemma <a href="#Thmtheorem5" title="Lemma 5. ‣ 5.2 From Polynomials to Their Coefficients ‣ 5 Critical Damping ‣ Critically-Damped Higher-Order Langevin Dynamics" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">5</span></a> implies</p>
<table id="S5.EGx14" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="S5.E9"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S5.E9.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle q(\lambda)=(-1)^{n}\sum_{k=0}^{\lfloor n/2\rfloor}\lambda^{n-2k}s_{n-1,k}-(-1)^{n-1}\xi\sum_{k=0}^{\lfloor(n-1)/2\rfloor}\lambda^{n-(2k+1)}s_{n-2,k}." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>q</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>λ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mi>n</mi></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">⌊</mo><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>/</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">⌋</mo></mrow></munderover></mstyle><mrow><msup><mi>λ</mi><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>−</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>s</mi><mrow><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo>,</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow></msub></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>ξ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">⌊</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>/</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">⌋</mo></mrow></munderover></mstyle><mrow><msup><mi>λ</mi><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>−</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>s</mi><mrow><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow><mo>,</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow></msub></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle q(\lambda)=(-1)^{n}\sum_{k=0}^{\lfloor n/2\rfloor}\lambda^{n-2k}s_{n-1,k}-(-1)^{n-1}\xi\sum_{k=0}^{\lfloor(n-1)/2\rfloor}\lambda^{n-(2k+1)}s_{n-2,k}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(9)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="S5.SS2.p4" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S5.SS2.p4.1" class="ltx_p">The following theorem is more general than the subject of this paper, and stated accordingly. Also, we remind the reader that a monic polynomial has leading coefficient 1.</p>
</div>
<div id="Thmtheorem6" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_theorem">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="Thmtheorem6.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Theorem 6</span></span><span id="Thmtheorem6.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="Thmtheorem6.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="Thmtheorem6.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="Thmtheorem6.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Let <math id="Thmtheorem6.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="m(x)=\sum_{k=0}^{n}a_{k}x^{k}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.111em">=</mo><mrow><msubsup><mo>∑</mo><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><mi>n</mi></msubsup><mrow><msub><mi>a</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>x</mi><mi>k</mi></msup></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">m(x)=\sum_{k=0}^{n}a_{k}x^{k}</annotation></semantics></math> be a degree-<math id="Thmtheorem6.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="n" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>n</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">n</annotation></semantics></math> monic polynomial. Then, <math id="Thmtheorem6.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="r" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>r</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">r</annotation></semantics></math> is a root of every derivative <math id="Thmtheorem6.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="m^{(j)}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>m</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>j</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">m^{(j)}</annotation></semantics></math> for <math id="Thmtheorem6.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="0\leq j\leq n-1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>≤</mo><mi>j</mi><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">0\leq j\leq n-1</annotation></semantics></math> if and only if every coefficient</span></p>
<table id="S5.EGx15" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="S5.Ex14"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S5.Ex14.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle a_{k}=\binom{n}{k}(-r)^{n-k}." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>a</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mo>(</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac linethickness="0pt"><mi>n</mi><mi>k</mi></mfrac></mstyle><mo>)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>r</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow></msup></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle a_{k}=\binom{n}{k}(-r)^{n-k}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
</div>
<div id="S5.SS2.p5" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S5.SS2.p5.1" class="ltx_p">Theorem <a href="#Thmtheorem6" title="Theorem 6. ‣ 5.2 From Polynomials to Their Coefficients ‣ 5 Critical Damping ‣ Critically-Damped Higher-Order Langevin Dynamics" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">6</span></a> can be restated as <math id="S5.SS2.p5.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="r" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>r</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">r</annotation></semantics></math> is a root of every non-constant derivative of <math id="S5.SS2.p5.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="m" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>m</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">m</annotation></semantics></math> if and only if <math id="S5.SS2.p5.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="r" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>r</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">r</annotation></semantics></math> is the unique root of <math id="S5.SS2.p5.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="m" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>m</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">m</annotation></semantics></math>.
This theorem is established in Appendix <a href="#A2" title="Appendix B Proof of Theorem ‣ Critically-Damped Higher-Order Langevin Dynamics" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">B</span></a>. Choosing <math id="S5.SS2.p5.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\lambda_{*}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>λ</mi><mo>∗</mo></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\lambda_{*}</annotation></semantics></math> as our root and matching terms from Theorem <a href="#Thmtheorem6" title="Theorem 6. ‣ 5.2 From Polynomials to Their Coefficients ‣ 5 Critical Damping ‣ Critically-Damped Higher-Order Langevin Dynamics" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">6</span></a> with Equation <a href="#S5.E9" title="In 5.2 From Polynomials to Their Coefficients ‣ 5 Critical Damping ‣ Critically-Damped Higher-Order Langevin Dynamics" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">9</span></a>, it is easy to see that</p>
<table id="S5.EGx16" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="S5.Ex15"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S5.Ex15.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle s_{n-1,k}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>s</mi><mrow><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo>,</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle s_{n-1,k}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S5.Ex15.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\binom{n}{2k}\lambda_{*}^{2k}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mo>(</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac linethickness="0pt"><mi>n</mi><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo>)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>λ</mi><mo>∗</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow></msubsup></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\binom{n}{2k}\lambda_{*}^{2k}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><span id="S5.Ex15.5.1" class="ltx_text ltx_markedasmath">and</span></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S5.Ex15.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\xi s_{n-2,k}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>ξ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>s</mi><mrow><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow><mo>,</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\xi s_{n-2,k}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S5.Ex15.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\binom{n}{2k+1}(-\lambda_{*})^{2k+1}." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mo>(</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac linethickness="0pt"><mi>n</mi><mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo>)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>λ</mi><mo>∗</mo></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\binom{n}{2k+1}(-\lambda_{*})^{2k+1}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S5.SS2.p5.2" class="ltx_p">Further, because <math id="S5.SS2.p5.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="s_{n-2,0}=1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>s</mi><mrow><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow><mo>,</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow></msub><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">s_{n-2,0}=1</annotation></semantics></math> as defined in Equation <a href="#S5.E8" title="In 5.2 From Polynomials to Their Coefficients ‣ 5 Critical Damping ‣ Critically-Damped Higher-Order Langevin Dynamics" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">8</span></a>, we have</p>
<table id="S5.EGx17" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="S5.Ex16"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S5.Ex16.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\xi=\xi s_{n-2,0}=-n\lambda_{*};" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>ξ</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>ξ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>s</mi><mrow><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow><mo>,</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow></msub></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>λ</mi><mo>∗</mo></msub></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>;</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\xi=\xi s_{n-2,0}=-n\lambda_{*};</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S5.SS2.p5.3" class="ltx_p">which allows rearranging to get</p>
<table id="S5.EGx18" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="S5.Ex17"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S5.Ex17.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle s_{n-2,k}=\binom{n}{2k+1}\frac{\lambda_{*}^{2k}}{n}=\frac{\binom{k+1}{k}}{\binom{2(k+1)}{2k}}\binom{n-1}{2k}\lambda_{*}^{2k}." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>s</mi><mrow><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow><mo>,</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mo>(</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac linethickness="0pt"><mi>n</mi><mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo>)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><msubsup><mi>λ</mi><mo>∗</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow></msubsup><mi>n</mi></mfrac></mstyle></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mo>(</mo><mfrac linethickness="0pt"><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>k</mi></mfrac><mo>)</mo></mrow><mrow><mo>(</mo><mfrac linethickness="0pt"><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow></mfrac><mo>)</mo></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac linethickness="0pt"><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo>)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>λ</mi><mo>∗</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow></msubsup></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle s_{n-2,k}=\binom{n}{2k+1}\frac{\lambda_{*}^{2k}}{n}=\frac{\binom{k+1}{k}}{\binom{2(k+1)}{2k}}\binom{n-1}{2k}\lambda_{*}^{2k}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S5.SS2.p5.4" class="ltx_p">More broadly, we observe the pattern and propose the following general form for <math id="S5.SS2.p5.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="s_{n-i,k}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>s</mi><mrow><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow><mo>,</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">s_{n-i,k}</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
<table id="S5.EGx19" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="S5.E10"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S5.E10.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle s_{n-i,k}=\frac{\binom{i+k-1}{k}}{\binom{2(i+k-1)}{2k}}\binom{n-i+1}{2k}\lambda_{*}^{2k}." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>s</mi><mrow><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow><mo>,</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mo>(</mo><mfrac linethickness="0pt"><mrow><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>k</mi></mfrac><mo>)</mo></mrow><mrow><mo>(</mo><mfrac linethickness="0pt"><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow></mfrac><mo>)</mo></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac linethickness="0pt"><mrow><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo>)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>λ</mi><mo>∗</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow></msubsup></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle s_{n-i,k}=\frac{\binom{i+k-1}{k}}{\binom{2(i+k-1)}{2k}}\binom{n-i+1}{2k}\lambda_{*}^{2k}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(10)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S5.SS2.p5.5" class="ltx_p">What we are really trying to do here is solve a difference equation proposed in Equation <a href="#S5.E8" title="In 5.2 From Polynomials to Their Coefficients ‣ 5 Critical Damping ‣ Critically-Damped Higher-Order Langevin Dynamics" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">8</span></a>. The sequence of <math id="S5.SS2.p5.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\gamma_{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>γ</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\gamma_{i}</annotation></semantics></math> are uniquely determined from the sequence <math id="S5.SS2.p5.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="s_{j,k}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>s</mi><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">s_{j,k}</annotation></semantics></math>, so if we solve for the resulting <math id="S5.SS2.p5.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\gamma_{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>γ</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\gamma_{i}</annotation></semantics></math>, then satisfy the recurrence relation in Equation <a href="#S5.E8" title="In 5.2 From Polynomials to Their Coefficients ‣ 5 Critical Damping ‣ Critically-Damped Higher-Order Langevin Dynamics" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">8</span></a>, then we have successfully solved the difference equation.</p>
</div>
<div id="Thmtheorem7" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_theorem">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="Thmtheorem7.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Theorem 7</span></span><span id="Thmtheorem7.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="Thmtheorem7.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="Thmtheorem7.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="Thmtheorem7.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Fix <math id="Thmtheorem7.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="n&gt;0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">n&gt;0</annotation></semantics></math>. For <math id="Thmtheorem7.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\{s_{j,k}\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><msub><mi>s</mi><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\{s_{j,k}\}</annotation></semantics></math> as defined in Equation <a href="#S5.E8" title="In 5.2 From Polynomials to Their Coefficients ‣ 5 Critical Damping ‣ Critically-Damped Higher-Order Langevin Dynamics" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">8</span></a>, if for <math id="Thmtheorem7.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="n-i&gt;2k-2" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow><mo>&gt;</mo><mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">n-i&gt;2k-2</annotation></semantics></math>,</span></p>
<table id="S5.EGx20" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="S5.Ex18"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S5.Ex18.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle s_{n-i,k}=\frac{\binom{i+k-1}{k}}{\binom{2(i+k-1)}{2k}}\binom{n-i+1}{2k}\lambda_{*}^{2k}." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>s</mi><mrow><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow><mo>,</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mo>(</mo><mfrac linethickness="0pt"><mrow><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>k</mi></mfrac><mo>)</mo></mrow><mrow><mo>(</mo><mfrac linethickness="0pt"><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow></mfrac><mo>)</mo></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac linethickness="0pt"><mrow><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo>)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>λ</mi><mo>∗</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow></msubsup></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle s_{n-i,k}=\frac{\binom{i+k-1}{k}}{\binom{2(i+k-1)}{2k}}\binom{n-i+1}{2k}\lambda_{*}^{2k}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="Thmtheorem7.p1.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="Thmtheorem7.p1.2.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">then</span></p>
<table id="S5.EGx21" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="S5.Ex19"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S5.Ex19.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\gamma_{n-i}^{2}=\frac{n^{2}-i^{2}}{4i^{2}-1}\lambda_{*}^{2}." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi>γ</mi><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo>=</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><msup><mi>n</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>−</mo><msup><mi>i</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><mrow><mrow><mn>4</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>i</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>λ</mi><mo>∗</mo><mn>2</mn></msubsup></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\gamma_{n-i}^{2}=\frac{n^{2}-i^{2}}{4i^{2}-1}\lambda_{*}^{2}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
</div>
<div id="Thmtheorem8" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_lemma">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="Thmtheorem8.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Lemma 8</span></span><span id="Thmtheorem8.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="Thmtheorem8.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="Thmtheorem8.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="Thmtheorem8.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Fix <math id="Thmtheorem8.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="n&gt;0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">n&gt;0</annotation></semantics></math>. The following <math id="Thmtheorem8.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="s_{n-i,k}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>s</mi><mrow><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow><mo>,</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">s_{n-i,k}</annotation></semantics></math>, for <math id="Thmtheorem8.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="n-i&gt;2k-2" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow><mo>&gt;</mo><mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">n-i&gt;2k-2</annotation></semantics></math>, satisfies the definition from Equation <a href="#S5.E8" title="In 5.2 From Polynomials to Their Coefficients ‣ 5 Critical Damping ‣ Critically-Damped Higher-Order Langevin Dynamics" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">8</span></a>.</span></p>
<table id="S5.EGx22" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="S5.Ex20"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S5.Ex20.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle s_{n-i,k}=\frac{\binom{i+k-1}{k}}{\binom{2(i+k-1)}{2k}}\binom{n-i+1}{2k}\lambda_{*}^{2k}." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>s</mi><mrow><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow><mo>,</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mo>(</mo><mfrac linethickness="0pt"><mrow><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>k</mi></mfrac><mo>)</mo></mrow><mrow><mo>(</mo><mfrac linethickness="0pt"><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow></mfrac><mo>)</mo></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac linethickness="0pt"><mrow><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo>)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>λ</mi><mo>∗</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow></msubsup></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle s_{n-i,k}=\frac{\binom{i+k-1}{k}}{\binom{2(i+k-1)}{2k}}\binom{n-i+1}{2k}\lambda_{*}^{2k}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
</div>
<div id="S5.SS2.p6" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S5.SS2.p6.1" class="ltx_p">Theorem <a href="#Thmtheorem7" title="Theorem 7. ‣ 5.2 From Polynomials to Their Coefficients ‣ 5 Critical Damping ‣ Critically-Damped Higher-Order Langevin Dynamics" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">7</span></a> and Lemma <a href="#Thmtheorem8" title="Lemma 8. ‣ 5.2 From Polynomials to Their Coefficients ‣ 5 Critical Damping ‣ Critically-Damped Higher-Order Langevin Dynamics" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">8</span></a> are proven in Appendices <a href="#A3" title="Appendix C Proof of Theorem ‣ Critically-Damped Higher-Order Langevin Dynamics" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">C</span></a> and <a href="#A4" title="Appendix D Proof of Lemma ‣ Critically-Damped Higher-Order Langevin Dynamics" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">D</span></a> respectively. This leads us quite easily to the following lemma.</p>
</div>
<div id="Thmtheorem9" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_lemma">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="Thmtheorem9.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Lemma 9</span></span><span id="Thmtheorem9.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="Thmtheorem9.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="Thmtheorem9.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="Thmtheorem9.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">The choice of <math id="Thmtheorem9.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\gamma_{1}=1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>γ</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\gamma_{1}=1</annotation></semantics></math> implies that</span></p>
<table id="S5.EGx23" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="S5.Ex21"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S5.Ex21.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\lambda_{*}=-\sqrt{2n-3}." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>λ</mi><mo>∗</mo></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo>−</mo><msqrt><mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>3</mn></mrow></msqrt></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\lambda_{*}=-\sqrt{2n-3}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
</div>
<div id="S5.SS2.2" class="ltx_proof">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_font_italic ltx_title_proof">Proof.</h6>
<div id="S5.SS2.p7" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S5.SS2.p7.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S5.SS2.p7.1.1" class="ltx_text">Using the formula in Theorem <a href="#Thmtheorem7" title="Theorem 7. ‣ 5.2 From Polynomials to Their Coefficients ‣ 5 Critical Damping ‣ Critically-Damped Higher-Order Langevin Dynamics" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">7</span></a></span></p>
<table id="S5.Ex22" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S5.Ex22.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="1=\gamma_{1}^{2}=\gamma_{n-(n-1)}^{2}=\frac{n^{2}-(n-1)^{2}}{4(n-1)^{2}-1}\lambda_{*}^{2}=\frac{\lambda_{*}^{2}}{2n-3}" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>=</mo><msubsup><mi>γ</mi><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo>=</mo><msubsup><mi>γ</mi><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>−</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo>=</mo><mrow><mfrac><mrow><msup><mi>n</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>−</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><mrow><mrow><mn>4</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>λ</mi><mo>∗</mo><mn>2</mn></msubsup></mrow><mo>=</mo><mfrac><msubsup><mi>λ</mi><mo>∗</mo><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>3</mn></mrow></mfrac></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">1=\gamma_{1}^{2}=\gamma_{n-(n-1)}^{2}=\frac{n^{2}-(n-1)^{2}}{4(n-1)^{2}-1}\lambda_{*}^{2}=\frac{\lambda_{*}^{2}}{2n-3}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="S5.SS2.p8" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S5.SS2.p8.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S5.SS2.p8.1.1" class="ltx_text">This directly implies <math id="S5.SS2.p8.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\lambda_{*}=-\sqrt{2n-3}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>λ</mi><mo>∗</mo></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo>−</mo><msqrt><mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>3</mn></mrow></msqrt></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\lambda_{*}=-\sqrt{2n-3}</annotation></semantics></math>, as <math id="S5.SS2.p8.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\lambda_{*}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>λ</mi><mo>∗</mo></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\lambda_{*}</annotation></semantics></math> is designed to be negative.</span></p>
</div>
<div id="S5.SS2.p9" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S5.SS2.p9.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S5.SS2.p9.1.1" class="ltx_text">∎</span></p>
</div>
</div>
</section>
</section>
<section id="A1" class="ltx_appendix">
<h2 class="ltx_title ltx_title_appendix"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_appendix">Appendix A </span>Proof of Lemma <a href="#Thmtheorem5" title="Lemma 5. ‣ 5.2 From Polynomials to Their Coefficients ‣ 5 Critical Damping ‣ Critically-Damped Higher-Order Langevin Dynamics" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">5</span></a></h2>

<div id="A1.2" class="ltx_proof">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_font_italic ltx_title_proof">Proof.</h6>
<div id="A1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text">The proof proceeds by induction on <math id="A1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="j" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>j</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">j</annotation></semantics></math>. The base case for <math id="A1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="d_{1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>d</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">d_{1}</annotation></semantics></math> is trivial, and because <math id="A1.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="s_{1,1}=\gamma_{1}^{2}s_{1,0}+s_{1,1}=\gamma_{1}^{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>s</mi><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi>γ</mi><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>s</mi><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow></msub></mrow><mo>+</mo><msub><mi>s</mi><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub></mrow><mo>=</mo><msubsup><mi>γ</mi><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></msubsup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">s_{1,1}=\gamma_{1}^{2}s_{1,0}+s_{1,1}=\gamma_{1}^{2}</annotation></semantics></math>,</span></p>
<table id="A1.EGx24" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A1.Ex23"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.Ex23.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle d_{2}(\lambda)=\lambda^{2}+\gamma_{1}^{2}=(-1)^{2}\sum_{k=0}^{1}\lambda^{2-2k}s_{1,k}." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>d</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>λ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><msup><mi>λ</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>+</mo><msubsup><mi>γ</mi><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></msubsup></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><mn>1</mn></munderover></mstyle><mrow><msup><mi>λ</mi><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo>−</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>s</mi><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow></msub></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle d_{2}(\lambda)=\lambda^{2}+\gamma_{1}^{2}=(-1)^{2}\sum_{k=0}^{1}\lambda^{2-2k}s_{1,k}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.p1.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.p1.2.1" class="ltx_text">Inductive Step:</span></p>
<table id="A1.Ex24" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.Ex24.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="d_{n+1}=-\lambda d_{n}+\gamma_{n-1}^{2}d_{n-1}" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>d</mi><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>λ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>d</mi><mi>n</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>γ</mi><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>d</mi><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">d_{n+1}=-\lambda d_{n}+\gamma_{n-1}^{2}d_{n-1}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<table id="A1.Ex25" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.Ex25.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="=-\lambda(-1)^{n}\sum_{k=0}^{\lfloor n/2\rfloor}\lambda^{n-2k}s_{n-1,k}+\gamma_{n-1}^{2}(-1)^{n-1}\sum_{k=0}^{\lfloor(n-1)/2\rfloor}\lambda^{n-2k-1}s_{n-2,k}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo rspace="0em">=</mo><mo lspace="0em">−</mo><mi>λ</mi><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo lspace="0em">−</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mi>n</mi></msup><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">⌊</mo><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>/</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">⌋</mo></mrow></munderover><msup><mi>λ</mi><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>−</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow></mrow></msup><msub><mi>s</mi><mrow><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo>,</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow></msub><mo>+</mo><msubsup><mi>γ</mi><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mn>2</mn></msubsup><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo lspace="0em">−</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">⌊</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>/</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">⌋</mo></mrow></munderover><msup><mi>λ</mi><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>−</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><msub><mi>s</mi><mrow><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow><mo>,</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">=-\lambda(-1)^{n}\sum_{k=0}^{\lfloor n/2\rfloor}\lambda^{n-2k}s_{n-1,k}+\gamma_{n-1}^{2}(-1)^{n-1}\sum_{k=0}^{\lfloor(n-1)/2\rfloor}\lambda^{n-2k-1}s_{n-2,k}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="A1.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.p2.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.p2.1.1" class="ltx_text">Now, we must break up cases into even and odd <math id="A1.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="n" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>n</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">n</annotation></semantics></math>:</span></p>
</div>
<div id="A1.p3" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A1.p3.1" class="ltx_p">Case <math id="A1.p3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="n" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>n</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">n</annotation></semantics></math> is even:
When this happens, <math id="A1.p3.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\lfloor\frac{n}{2}\rfloor=\frac{n}{2},\lfloor\frac{n-1}{2}\rfloor=\frac{n}{2}-1,\lfloor\frac{n+1}{2}\rfloor=\frac{n}{2}," display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">⌊</mo><mfrac><mi>n</mi><mn>2</mn></mfrac><mo stretchy="false">⌋</mo></mrow><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mi>n</mi><mn>2</mn></mfrac></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">⌊</mo><mfrac><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mn>2</mn></mfrac><mo stretchy="false">⌋</mo></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mfrac><mi>n</mi><mn>2</mn></mfrac><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">⌊</mo><mfrac><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mn>2</mn></mfrac><mo stretchy="false">⌋</mo></mrow><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mi>n</mi><mn>2</mn></mfrac></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\lfloor\frac{n}{2}\rfloor=\frac{n}{2},\lfloor\frac{n-1}{2}\rfloor=\frac{n}{2}-1,\lfloor\frac{n+1}{2}\rfloor=\frac{n}{2},</annotation></semantics></math></p>
<table id="A1.Ex26" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.Ex26.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="d_{n+1}=\lambda(-1)^{n-1}\sum_{k=0}^{n/2}\lambda^{n-2k}s_{n-1,k}+\gamma_{n-1}^{2}(-1)^{n-1}\sum_{k=0}^{n/2-1}\lambda^{n-2k-1}s_{n-2,k}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>d</mi><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>λ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>/</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></munderover><mrow><msup><mi>λ</mi><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>−</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>s</mi><mrow><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo>,</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow></msub></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>γ</mi><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>/</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></munderover><mrow><msup><mi>λ</mi><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>−</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>s</mi><mrow><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow><mo>,</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow></msub></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">d_{n+1}=\lambda(-1)^{n-1}\sum_{k=0}^{n/2}\lambda^{n-2k}s_{n-1,k}+\gamma_{n-1}^{2}(-1)^{n-1}\sum_{k=0}^{n/2-1}\lambda^{n-2k-1}s_{n-2,k}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="A1.p4" class="ltx_para ltx_indent">
<p id="A1.p4.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.p4.1.1" class="ltx_text">Then by reindexing the second sum, and noting <math id="A1.p4.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(-1)^{n-1}=(-1)^{n+1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mo>=</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(-1)^{n-1}=(-1)^{n+1}</annotation></semantics></math>:</span></p>
<table id="A1.Ex27" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.Ex27.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="d_{n+1}=(-1)^{n+1}\sum_{k=0}^{n/2}\lambda^{n-2k+1}s_{n-1,k}+\gamma_{n-1}^{2}(-1)^{n+1}\sum_{k=1}^{n/2}\lambda^{n-2k+1}s_{n-2,k-1}" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>d</mi><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>/</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></munderover><mrow><msup><mi>λ</mi><mrow><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>−</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>s</mi><mrow><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo>,</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow></msub></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>γ</mi><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>/</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></munderover><mrow><msup><mi>λ</mi><mrow><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>−</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>s</mi><mrow><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mrow></msub></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">d_{n+1}=(-1)^{n+1}\sum_{k=0}^{n/2}\lambda^{n-2k+1}s_{n-1,k}+\gamma_{n-1}^{2}(-1)^{n+1}\sum_{k=1}^{n/2}\lambda^{n-2k+1}s_{n-2,k-1}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<table id="A1.Ex28" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.Ex28.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="=(-1)^{n+1}\sum_{k=0}^{n/2}\lambda^{(n+1)-2k}\left(s_{n-1,k}+\gamma_{n-1}^{2}s_{n-2,k-1}\right)." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>/</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></munderover><mrow><msup><mi>λ</mi><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>s</mi><mrow><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo>,</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow></msub><mo>+</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>γ</mi><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>s</mi><mrow><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mrow></msub></mrow></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">=(-1)^{n+1}\sum_{k=0}^{n/2}\lambda^{(n+1)-2k}\left(s_{n-1,k}+\gamma_{n-1}^{2}s_{n-2,k-1}\right).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.p4.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.p4.2.1" class="ltx_text">By the sequence definition:</span></p>
<table id="A1.Ex29" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.Ex29.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="=(-1)^{n+1}\sum_{k=0}^{\lfloor(n+1)/2\rfloor}\lambda^{(n+1)-2k}s_{n,k}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">⌊</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>/</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">⌋</mo></mrow></munderover><mrow><msup><mi>λ</mi><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>s</mi><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow></msub></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">=(-1)^{n+1}\sum_{k=0}^{\lfloor(n+1)/2\rfloor}\lambda^{(n+1)-2k}s_{n,k}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="A1.p5" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A1.p5.1" class="ltx_p">Case <math id="A1.p5.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="n" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>n</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">n</annotation></semantics></math> is odd: When this happens, <math id="A1.p5.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\lfloor\frac{n}{2}\rfloor=\frac{n-1}{2},\lfloor\frac{n-1}{2}\rfloor=\frac{n-1}{2},\lfloor\frac{n+1}{2}\rfloor=\frac{n+1}{2}," display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">⌊</mo><mfrac><mi>n</mi><mn>2</mn></mfrac><mo stretchy="false">⌋</mo></mrow><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mn>2</mn></mfrac></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">⌊</mo><mfrac><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mn>2</mn></mfrac><mo stretchy="false">⌋</mo></mrow><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mn>2</mn></mfrac></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">⌊</mo><mfrac><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mn>2</mn></mfrac><mo stretchy="false">⌋</mo></mrow><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mn>2</mn></mfrac></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\lfloor\frac{n}{2}\rfloor=\frac{n-1}{2},\lfloor\frac{n-1}{2}\rfloor=\frac{n-1}{2},\lfloor\frac{n+1}{2}\rfloor=\frac{n+1}{2},</annotation></semantics></math></p>
</div>
<div id="A1.p6" class="ltx_para">
<table id="A1.Ex30" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.Ex30.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="d_{n+1}=\lambda(-1)^{n+1}\sum_{k=0}^{(n-1)/2}\lambda^{n-2k}s_{n-1,k}+\gamma_{n-1}^{2}(-1)^{n+1}\sum_{k=0}^{(n-1)/2}\lambda^{n-2k-1}s_{n-2,k}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>d</mi><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>λ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>/</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></munderover><mrow><msup><mi>λ</mi><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>−</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>s</mi><mrow><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo>,</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow></msub></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>γ</mi><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>/</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></munderover><mrow><msup><mi>λ</mi><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>−</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>s</mi><mrow><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow><mo>,</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow></msub></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">d_{n+1}=\lambda(-1)^{n+1}\sum_{k=0}^{(n-1)/2}\lambda^{n-2k}s_{n-1,k}+\gamma_{n-1}^{2}(-1)^{n+1}\sum_{k=0}^{(n-1)/2}\lambda^{n-2k-1}s_{n-2,k}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="A1.p7" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.p7.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.p7.1.1" class="ltx_text">Once again reindexing the second sum:</span></p>
<table id="A1.Ex31" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.Ex31.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="=(-1)^{n+1}\sum_{k=0}^{(n-1)/2}\lambda^{n-2k+1}s_{n-1,k}+\gamma_{n-1}^{2}(-1)^{n+1}\sum_{k=1}^{(n+1)/2}\lambda^{n-2k+1}s_{n-2,k-1}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>/</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></munderover><mrow><msup><mi>λ</mi><mrow><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>−</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>s</mi><mrow><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo>,</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow></msub></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>γ</mi><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>/</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></munderover><mrow><msup><mi>λ</mi><mrow><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>−</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>s</mi><mrow><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mrow></msub></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">=(-1)^{n+1}\sum_{k=0}^{(n-1)/2}\lambda^{n-2k+1}s_{n-1,k}+\gamma_{n-1}^{2}(-1)^{n+1}\sum_{k=1}^{(n+1)/2}\lambda^{n-2k+1}s_{n-2,k-1}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="A1.p8" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.p8.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.p8.1.1" class="ltx_text">By adding and subtracting the final term of the sum:</span></p>
<table id="A1.Ex32" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.Ex32.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="=(-1)^{n+1}\left(\sum_{k=0}^{(n+1)/2}\left(\lambda^{n-2k+1}s_{n-1,k}\right)-\lambda^{0}s_{n-1,(n+1)/2}\right)+\gamma_{n-1}^{2}(-1)^{n+1}\sum_{k=1}^{(n+1)/2}\lambda^{n-2k+1}s_{n-2,k-1}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mrow><munderover><mo lspace="0em" movablelimits="false" rspace="0em">∑</mo><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>/</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></munderover><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><msup><mi>λ</mi><mrow><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>−</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>s</mi><mrow><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo>,</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msup><mi>λ</mi><mn>0</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>s</mi><mrow><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>/</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></mrow></msub></mrow></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>γ</mi><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>/</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></munderover><mrow><msup><mi>λ</mi><mrow><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>−</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>s</mi><mrow><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mrow></msub></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">=(-1)^{n+1}\left(\sum_{k=0}^{(n+1)/2}\left(\lambda^{n-2k+1}s_{n-1,k}\right)-\lambda^{0}s_{n-1,(n+1)/2}\right)+\gamma_{n-1}^{2}(-1)^{n+1}\sum_{k=1}^{(n+1)/2}\lambda^{n-2k+1}s_{n-2,k-1}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="A1.p9" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.p9.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.p9.1.1" class="ltx_text">However, note that <math id="A1.p9.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="s_{n-1,(n+1)/2}=0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>s</mi><mrow><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>/</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></mrow></msub><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">s_{n-1,(n+1)/2}=0</annotation></semantics></math>, thus the <math id="A1.p9.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\lambda^{0}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>λ</mi><mn>0</mn></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\lambda^{0}</annotation></semantics></math> term cancels anyway. Thus we have:</span></p>
</div>
<div id="A1.p10" class="ltx_para">
<table id="A1.Ex33" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.Ex33.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="=(-1)^{n+1}\sum_{k=0}^{(n+1)/2}\lambda^{n-2k+1}\left(s_{n-1,k}+\gamma_{n-1}^{2}s_{n-2,k-1}\right)." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>/</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></munderover><mrow><msup><mi>λ</mi><mrow><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>−</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>s</mi><mrow><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo>,</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow></msub><mo>+</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>γ</mi><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>s</mi><mrow><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mrow></msub></mrow></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">=(-1)^{n+1}\sum_{k=0}^{(n+1)/2}\lambda^{n-2k+1}\left(s_{n-1,k}+\gamma_{n-1}^{2}s_{n-2,k-1}\right).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="A1.p11" class="ltx_para ltx_indent">
<p id="A1.p11.1" class="ltx_p">By the sequence definition:</p>
<table id="A1.Ex34" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.Ex34.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="=(-1)^{n+1}\sum_{k=0}^{\lfloor(n+1)/2\rfloor}\lambda^{(n+1)-2k}s_{n,k}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">⌊</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>/</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">⌋</mo></mrow></munderover><mrow><msup><mi>λ</mi><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>s</mi><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow></msub></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">=(-1)^{n+1}\sum_{k=0}^{\lfloor(n+1)/2\rfloor}\lambda^{(n+1)-2k}s_{n,k}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="A1.p12" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.p12.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.p12.1.1" class="ltx_text">∎</span></p>
</div>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A2" class="ltx_appendix">
<h2 class="ltx_title ltx_title_appendix"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_appendix">Appendix B </span>Proof of Theorem <a href="#Thmtheorem6" title="Theorem 6. ‣ 5.2 From Polynomials to Their Coefficients ‣ 5 Critical Damping ‣ Critically-Damped Higher-Order Langevin Dynamics" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">6</span></a></h2>

<div id="A2.2" class="ltx_proof">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_font_italic ltx_title_proof">Proof.</h6>
<div id="A2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text">Starting with the converse, if <math id="A2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="a_{k}=\binom{n}{k}(-r)^{n-k}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>a</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mo>(</mo><mfrac linethickness="0pt"><mi>n</mi><mi>k</mi></mfrac><mo>)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>r</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow></msup></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">a_{k}=\binom{n}{k}(-r)^{n-k}</annotation></semantics></math>, then the Binomial Theorem implies</span></p>
<table id="A2.EGx25" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A2.Ex35"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.Ex35.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle p(x)=\sum_{k=0}^{n}a_{k}x^{k}=\sum_{k=0}^{n}\binom{n}{k}(-r)^{n-k}x^{k}=(x-r)^{n}." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><mi>n</mi></munderover></mstyle><mrow><msub><mi>a</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>x</mi><mi>k</mi></msup></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><mi>n</mi></munderover></mstyle><mrow><mrow><mo>(</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac linethickness="0pt"><mi>n</mi><mi>k</mi></mfrac></mstyle><mo>)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>r</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>x</mi><mi>k</mi></msup></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>r</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mi>n</mi></msup></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle p(x)=\sum_{k=0}^{n}a_{k}x^{k}=\sum_{k=0}^{n}\binom{n}{k}(-r)^{n-k}x^{k}=(x-r)^{n}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.p1.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.p1.2.1" class="ltx_text">Clearly, the <math id="A2.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="j" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>j</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">j</annotation></semantics></math>th derivative has <math id="A2.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="r" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>r</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">r</annotation></semantics></math> as a root for <math id="A2.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="j\in\{0,\ldots,n-1\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">j\in\{0,\ldots,n-1\}</annotation></semantics></math>.</span></p>
</div>
<div id="A2.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.p2.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.p2.1.1" class="ltx_text">To establish sufficiency, assume that <math id="A2.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="r" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>r</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">r</annotation></semantics></math> is a root of <math id="A2.p2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p^{(n-j)}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>p</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p^{(n-j)}</annotation></semantics></math> for every <math id="A2.p2.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="1\leq j\leq n" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>≤</mo><mi>j</mi><mo>≤</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">1\leq j\leq n</annotation></semantics></math>. Also, remember from first principles that</span></p>
<table id="A2.EGx26" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A2.E11"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.E11.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle p^{(n-j)}(x)=\sum_{k=0}^{j}\frac{(n-k)!}{(j-k)!}a_{n-k}x^{j-k}." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>p</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><mi>j</mi></munderover></mstyle><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>!</mo></mrow><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>!</mo></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>a</mi><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>x</mi><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow></msup></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle p^{(n-j)}(x)=\sum_{k=0}^{j}\frac{(n-k)!}{(j-k)!}a_{n-k}x^{j-k}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(11)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.p2.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.p2.2.1" class="ltx_text">Of course, <math id="A2.p2.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>p</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p</annotation></semantics></math> is monic by construction, so <math id="A2.p2.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="a_{n}=1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>a</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">a_{n}=1</annotation></semantics></math>.
Now, suppose strongly that <math id="A2.p2.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="a_{n-k}=\binom{n}{k}(-r)^{k}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>a</mi><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mo>(</mo><mfrac linethickness="0pt"><mi>n</mi><mi>k</mi></mfrac><mo>)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>r</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mi>k</mi></msup></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">a_{n-k}=\binom{n}{k}(-r)^{k}</annotation></semantics></math> for <math id="A2.p2.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="k&lt;j" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>&lt;</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">k&lt;j</annotation></semantics></math>.
Then, rearranging Equation <a href="#A2.E11" title="In Proof. ‣ Appendix B Proof of Theorem ‣ Critically-Damped Higher-Order Langevin Dynamics" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">11</span></a> and using the root assumption gives</span></p>
<table id="A2.EGx27" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A2.Ex36"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.Ex36.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle a_{n-j}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>a</mi><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle a_{n-j}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.Ex36.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\frac{p^{(n-j)}(r)}{(n-j)!}-\frac{1}{(n-j)!}\sum_{k=0}^{j-1}\frac{(n-k)!}{(j-k)!}a_{n-k}r^{j-k}," display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><msup><mi>p</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>r</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>!</mo></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo>−</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>!</mo></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></munderover></mstyle><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>!</mo></mrow><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>!</mo></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>a</mi><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>r</mi><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow></msup></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\frac{p^{(n-j)}(r)}{(n-j)!}-\frac{1}{(n-j)!}\sum_{k=0}^{j-1}\frac{(n-k)!}{(j-k)!}a_{n-k}r^{j-k},</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A2.Ex37"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.Ex37.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle=-\frac{r^{j}}{(n-j)!}\sum_{k=0}^{j-1}\frac{n!}{(j-k)!k!}(-1)^{k}," display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo rspace="0em">=</mo><mo lspace="0em">−</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><msup><mi>r</mi><mi>j</mi></msup><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>!</mo></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></munderover></mstyle><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>!</mo></mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>!</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow><mo>!</mo></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo lspace="0em">−</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mi>k</mi></msup><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=-\frac{r^{j}}{(n-j)!}\sum_{k=0}^{j-1}\frac{n!}{(j-k)!k!}(-1)^{k},</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A2.Ex38"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.Ex38.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle=-\binom{n}{j}r^{j}\sum_{k=0}^{j-1}\binom{j}{k}(-1)^{k}," display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo rspace="0em">=</mo><mo lspace="0em">−</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac linethickness="0pt"><mi>n</mi><mi>j</mi></mfrac></mstyle><mo>)</mo></mrow><msup><mi>r</mi><mi>j</mi></msup><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></munderover></mstyle><mrow><mo>(</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac linethickness="0pt"><mi>j</mi><mi>k</mi></mfrac></mstyle><mo>)</mo></mrow><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo lspace="0em">−</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mi>k</mi></msup><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=-\binom{n}{j}r^{j}\sum_{k=0}^{j-1}\binom{j}{k}(-1)^{k},</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A2.Ex39"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.Ex39.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\binom{n}{j}(-r)^{j}." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mo>(</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac linethickness="0pt"><mi>n</mi><mi>j</mi></mfrac></mstyle><mo>)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>r</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mi>j</mi></msup></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\binom{n}{j}(-r)^{j}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.p2.3" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.p2.3.1" class="ltx_text">The last step in the preceding equation is due to the Binomial Theorem and the result follows by induction.
∎</span></p>
</div>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A3" class="ltx_appendix">
<h2 class="ltx_title ltx_title_appendix"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_appendix">Appendix C </span>Proof of Theorem <a href="#Thmtheorem7" title="Theorem 7. ‣ 5.2 From Polynomials to Their Coefficients ‣ 5 Critical Damping ‣ Critically-Damped Higher-Order Langevin Dynamics" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">7</span></a></h2>

<div id="A3.2" class="ltx_proof">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_font_italic ltx_title_proof">Proof.</h6>
<div id="A3.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A3.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text">In the case that <math id="A3.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="n-i&gt;2k-2" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow><mo>&gt;</mo><mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">n-i&gt;2k-2</annotation></semantics></math>, the values of <math id="A3.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\gamma_{n-i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>γ</mi><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\gamma_{n-i}</annotation></semantics></math> may be algebraically solved for in terms of the <math id="A3.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="s_{n-i,k}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>s</mi><mrow><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow><mo>,</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">s_{n-i,k}</annotation></semantics></math> as:</span></p>
</div>
<div id="A3.p2" class="ltx_para">
<table id="A3.Ex40" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A3.Ex40.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\gamma_{n-i}^{2}=\frac{s_{n-i,k}-s_{n-(i+1),k}}{s_{n-(i+2),k-1}}" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi>γ</mi><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><msub><mi>s</mi><mrow><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow><mo>,</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow></msub><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>s</mi><mrow><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>−</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><msub><mi>s</mi><mrow><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>−</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mrow></msub></mfrac></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\gamma_{n-i}^{2}=\frac{s_{n-i,k}-s_{n-(i+1),k}}{s_{n-(i+2),k-1}}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A3.p2.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.p2.1.1" class="ltx_text">With brute force, and using the proposed expression: <math id="A3.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="s_{n-i,k}=\frac{\binom{i+k-1}{k}}{\binom{2(i+k-1)}{2k}}\binom{n-i+1}{2k}\lambda_{*}^{2k}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>s</mi><mrow><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow><mo>,</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mfrac><mrow><mo>(</mo><mfrac linethickness="0pt"><mrow><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>k</mi></mfrac><mo>)</mo></mrow><mrow><mo>(</mo><mfrac linethickness="0pt"><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow></mfrac><mo>)</mo></mrow></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mfrac linethickness="0pt"><mrow><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow></mfrac><mo>)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>λ</mi><mo>∗</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow></msubsup></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">s_{n-i,k}=\frac{\binom{i+k-1}{k}}{\binom{2(i+k-1)}{2k}}\binom{n-i+1}{2k}\lambda_{*}^{2k}</annotation></semantics></math>, the numerator’s expression may be solved for as:</span></p>
</div>
<div id="A3.p3" class="ltx_para">
<table id="A3.Ex41" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A3.Ex41.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="s_{n-i,k}-s_{n-(i+1),k}=\lambda_{*}^{2k}\frac{\binom{i+k-1}{k}\binom{n-i}{2k}}{\binom{2(i+k-1)}{2k}}\left(\frac{2k(n+i)}{(n-i-2k+1)(2i+2k-1)}\right)." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>s</mi><mrow><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow><mo>,</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow></msub><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>s</mi><mrow><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>−</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>λ</mi><mo>∗</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mfrac><mrow><mrow><mo>(</mo><mfrac linethickness="0pt"><mrow><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>k</mi></mfrac><mo>)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mfrac linethickness="0pt"><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow></mfrac><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><mrow><mo>(</mo><mfrac linethickness="0pt"><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow></mfrac><mo>)</mo></mrow></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mfrac><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>k</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>i</mi><mo>−</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mfrac><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">s_{n-i,k}-s_{n-(i+1),k}=\lambda_{*}^{2k}\frac{\binom{i+k-1}{k}\binom{n-i}{2k}}{\binom{2(i+k-1)}{2k}}\left(\frac{2k(n+i)}{(n-i-2k+1)(2i+2k-1)}\right).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A3.p3.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.p3.1.1" class="ltx_text">Upon dividing the denominator’s expression, <math id="A3.p3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\gamma_{n-i}^{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi>γ</mi><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow><mn>2</mn></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\gamma_{n-i}^{2}</annotation></semantics></math> becomes:</span></p>
</div>
<div id="A3.p4" class="ltx_para">
<table id="A3.Ex42" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A3.Ex42.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\gamma_{n-i}^{2}=\lambda_{*}^{2}\frac{\binom{i+k-1}{k}}{\binom{i+k}{k-1}}\frac{\binom{2(i+k)}{2k-2}}{\binom{2(i+k-1)}{2k}}\frac{\binom{n-i}{2k}}{\binom{n-i-1}{2(k-1)}}\left(\frac{2k(n+i)}{(n-i-2k+1)(2i+2k-1)}\right)" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi>γ</mi><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo>=</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>λ</mi><mo>∗</mo><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mfrac><mrow><mo>(</mo><mfrac linethickness="0pt"><mrow><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>k</mi></mfrac><mo>)</mo></mrow><mrow><mo>(</mo><mfrac linethickness="0pt"><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mfrac><mo>)</mo></mrow></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mfrac><mrow><mo>(</mo><mfrac linethickness="0pt"><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></mfrac><mo>)</mo></mrow><mrow><mo>(</mo><mfrac linethickness="0pt"><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow></mfrac><mo>)</mo></mrow></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mfrac><mrow><mo>(</mo><mfrac linethickness="0pt"><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow></mfrac><mo>)</mo></mrow><mrow><mo>(</mo><mfrac linethickness="0pt"><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>i</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mfrac><mo>)</mo></mrow></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mfrac><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>k</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>i</mi><mo>−</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mfrac><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\gamma_{n-i}^{2}=\lambda_{*}^{2}\frac{\binom{i+k-1}{k}}{\binom{i+k}{k-1}}\frac{\binom{2(i+k)}{2k-2}}{\binom{2(i+k-1)}{2k}}\frac{\binom{n-i}{2k}}{\binom{n-i-1}{2(k-1)}}\left(\frac{2k(n+i)}{(n-i-2k+1)(2i+2k-1)}\right)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A3.p4.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.p4.1.1" class="ltx_text">Upon simplifying each binomial coefficient, the expression greatly simplifies:</span></p>
</div>
<div id="A3.p5" class="ltx_para">
<table id="A3.Ex43" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A3.Ex43.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\gamma_{n-i}^{2}=\lambda_{*}^{2}\frac{(2i+2k-1)(n-i)(n-i-2k+1)}{2k(2i+1)(2i-1)}\left(\frac{2k(n+i)}{(n-i-2k+1)(2i+2k-1)}\right)" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi>γ</mi><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo>=</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>λ</mi><mo>∗</mo><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mfrac><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>i</mi><mo>−</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>k</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mfrac><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>k</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>i</mi><mo>−</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mfrac><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\gamma_{n-i}^{2}=\lambda_{*}^{2}\frac{(2i+2k-1)(n-i)(n-i-2k+1)}{2k(2i+1)(2i-1)}\left(\frac{2k(n+i)}{(n-i-2k+1)(2i+2k-1)}\right)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="A3.p6" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A3.p6.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.p6.1.1" class="ltx_text">Obvious cancellations may be observed and interestingly enough, all factors involving <math id="A3.p6.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="k" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>k</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">k</annotation></semantics></math> cancel out, leaving us with:</span></p>
</div>
<div id="A3.p7" class="ltx_para">
<table id="A3.Ex44" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A3.Ex44.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\gamma_{n-i}^{2}=\frac{(n-i)(n+i)}{(2i+1)(2i-1)}\lambda_{*}^{2}=\frac{n^{2}-i^{2}}{4i^{2}-1}\lambda_{*}^{2}" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi>γ</mi><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo>=</mo><mrow><mfrac><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>λ</mi><mo>∗</mo><mn>2</mn></msubsup></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mfrac><mrow><msup><mi>n</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>−</mo><msup><mi>i</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><mrow><mrow><mn>4</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>i</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>λ</mi><mo>∗</mo><mn>2</mn></msubsup></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\gamma_{n-i}^{2}=\frac{(n-i)(n+i)}{(2i+1)(2i-1)}\lambda_{*}^{2}=\frac{n^{2}-i^{2}}{4i^{2}-1}\lambda_{*}^{2}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="A3.p8" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A3.p8.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.p8.1.1" class="ltx_text">∎</span></p>
</div>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A4" class="ltx_appendix">
<h2 class="ltx_title ltx_title_appendix"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_appendix">Appendix D </span>Proof of Lemma <a href="#Thmtheorem8" title="Lemma 8. ‣ 5.2 From Polynomials to Their Coefficients ‣ 5 Critical Damping ‣ Critically-Damped Higher-Order Langevin Dynamics" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">8</span></a></h2>

<div id="A4.2" class="ltx_proof">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_font_italic ltx_title_proof">Proof.</h6>
<div id="A4.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A4.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A4.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text">We establish that Equation <a href="#S5.E10" title="In 5.2 From Polynomials to Their Coefficients ‣ 5 Critical Damping ‣ Critically-Damped Higher-Order Langevin Dynamics" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">10</span></a> together with Theorem <a href="#Thmtheorem7" title="Theorem 7. ‣ 5.2 From Polynomials to Their Coefficients ‣ 5 Critical Damping ‣ Critically-Damped Higher-Order Langevin Dynamics" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">7</span></a> is a solution to the recurrence in Equation <a href="#S5.E8" title="In 5.2 From Polynomials to Their Coefficients ‣ 5 Critical Damping ‣ Critically-Damped Higher-Order Langevin Dynamics" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">8</span></a>.
This is a matter of simple combinatorial arithmetic,</span></p>
<table id="A4.EGx28" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A4.Ex45"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A4.Ex45.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\gamma^{2}_{n-i}s_{n-i-2,k-1}+s_{n-i-1,k}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi>γ</mi><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>s</mi><mrow><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>i</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mrow></msub></mrow><mo>+</mo><msub><mi>s</mi><mrow><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>i</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo>,</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\gamma^{2}_{n-i}s_{n-i-2,k-1}+s_{n-i-1,k}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A4.Ex45.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\frac{n^{2}-i^{2}}{4i^{2}-1}\frac{\binom{i+k}{k-1}}{\binom{2(i+k)}{2k-2}}\binom{n-i-1}{2k-2}\lambda_{*}^{2k}+\frac{\binom{i+k}{k}}{\binom{2(i+k)}{2k}}\binom{n-i-1}{2k}\lambda_{*}^{2k}," display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><msup><mi>n</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>−</mo><msup><mi>i</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><mrow><mrow><mn>4</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>i</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mo>(</mo><mfrac linethickness="0pt"><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mfrac><mo>)</mo></mrow><mrow><mo>(</mo><mfrac linethickness="0pt"><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></mfrac><mo>)</mo></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac linethickness="0pt"><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>i</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo>)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>λ</mi><mo>∗</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow></msubsup></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mo>(</mo><mfrac linethickness="0pt"><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow><mi>k</mi></mfrac><mo>)</mo></mrow><mrow><mo>(</mo><mfrac linethickness="0pt"><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow></mfrac><mo>)</mo></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac linethickness="0pt"><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>i</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo>)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>λ</mi><mo>∗</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow></msubsup></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\frac{n^{2}-i^{2}}{4i^{2}-1}\frac{\binom{i+k}{k-1}}{\binom{2(i+k)}{2k-2}}\binom{n-i-1}{2k-2}\lambda_{*}^{2k}+\frac{\binom{i+k}{k}}{\binom{2(i+k)}{2k}}\binom{n-i-1}{2k}\lambda_{*}^{2k},</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A4.Ex46"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A4.Ex46.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\frac{\binom{i+k-1}{k}}{\binom{2(i+k-1)}{2k}}\left[\frac{n+i}{2(i+k)-1}\binom{n-i}{2k-1}+\frac{2i-1}{2(i+k)-1}\binom{n-i}{2k}\right]\lambda_{*}^{2k}." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mo>(</mo><mfrac linethickness="0pt"><mrow><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>k</mi></mfrac><mo>)</mo></mrow><mrow><mo>(</mo><mfrac linethickness="0pt"><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow></mfrac><mo>)</mo></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><mrow><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow><mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac linethickness="0pt"><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow><mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac linethickness="0pt"><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>]</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>λ</mi><mo>∗</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow></msubsup></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\frac{\binom{i+k-1}{k}}{\binom{2(i+k-1)}{2k}}\left[\frac{n+i}{2(i+k)-1}\binom{n-i}{2k-1}+\frac{2i-1}{2(i+k)-1}\binom{n-i}{2k}\right]\lambda_{*}^{2k}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="A4.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A4.p2.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A4.p2.1.1" class="ltx_text">Focusing on the second summand, we rearrange to get</span></p>
<table id="A4.EGx29" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A4.Ex47"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A4.Ex47.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\frac{2i-1}{2(i+k)-1}\binom{n-i}{2k}=\left[1-\frac{2k}{2(i+k)-1}\right]\binom{n-i}{2k}=\binom{n-i}{2k}-\frac{n-i-2k+1}{2(i+k)-1}\binom{n-i}{2k-1}." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac linethickness="0pt"><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mo>[</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow><mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mfrac></mstyle></mrow><mo>]</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac linethickness="0pt"><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mo>(</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac linethickness="0pt"><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo>)</mo></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>i</mi><mo>−</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac linethickness="0pt"><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow><mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\frac{2i-1}{2(i+k)-1}\binom{n-i}{2k}=\left[1-\frac{2k}{2(i+k)-1}\right]\binom{n-i}{2k}=\binom{n-i}{2k}-\frac{n-i-2k+1}{2(i+k)-1}\binom{n-i}{2k-1}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A4.p2.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A4.p2.2.1" class="ltx_text">Substituting this form back in, and simplfiying gives</span></p>
<table id="A4.EGx30" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A4.Ex48"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A4.Ex48.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\gamma^{2}_{n-i}s_{n-i-2,k-1}+s_{n-i-1,k}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi>γ</mi><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>s</mi><mrow><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>i</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mrow></msub></mrow><mo>+</mo><msub><mi>s</mi><mrow><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>i</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo>,</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\gamma^{2}_{n-i}s_{n-i-2,k-1}+s_{n-i-1,k}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A4.Ex48.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\frac{\binom{i+k-1}{k}}{\binom{2(i+k-1)}{2k}}\left[\binom{n-i}{2k}+\binom{n-i}{2k-1}\right]\lambda_{*}^{2k}," display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mo>(</mo><mfrac linethickness="0pt"><mrow><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>k</mi></mfrac><mo>)</mo></mrow><mrow><mo>(</mo><mfrac linethickness="0pt"><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow></mfrac><mo>)</mo></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><mrow><mrow><mo>(</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac linethickness="0pt"><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo>)</mo></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac linethickness="0pt"><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow><mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>]</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>λ</mi><mo>∗</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow></msubsup></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\frac{\binom{i+k-1}{k}}{\binom{2(i+k-1)}{2k}}\left[\binom{n-i}{2k}+\binom{n-i}{2k-1}\right]\lambda_{*}^{2k},</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A4.Ex49"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A4.Ex49.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\frac{\binom{i+k-1}{k}}{\binom{2(i+k-1)}{2k}}\binom{n-i+1}{2k}\lambda_{*}^{2k}," display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mo>(</mo><mfrac linethickness="0pt"><mrow><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>k</mi></mfrac><mo>)</mo></mrow><mrow><mo>(</mo><mfrac linethickness="0pt"><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow></mfrac><mo>)</mo></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac linethickness="0pt"><mrow><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo>)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>λ</mi><mo>∗</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow></msubsup></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\frac{\binom{i+k-1}{k}}{\binom{2(i+k-1)}{2k}}\binom{n-i+1}{2k}\lambda_{*}^{2k},</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A4.Ex50"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A4.Ex50.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=s_{n-i,k}." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>s</mi><mrow><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow><mo>,</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=s_{n-i,k}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A4.p2.3" class="ltx_p"><span id="A4.p2.3.1" class="ltx_text">Of course, if <math id="A4.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="n-i\leq 2k-2" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">n-i\leq 2k-2</annotation></semantics></math> then <math id="A4.p2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\binom{n-i+1}{2k}=0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo>(</mo><mfrac linethickness="0pt"><mrow><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow></mfrac><mo>)</mo></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\binom{n-i+1}{2k}=0</annotation></semantics></math>; otherwise, we can easily verify that <math id="A4.p2.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="s_{n-i,0}=1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>s</mi><mrow><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow><mo>,</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow></msub><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">s_{n-i,0}=1</annotation></semantics></math>.
So, Equation <a href="#S5.E10" title="In 5.2 From Polynomials to Their Coefficients ‣ 5 Critical Damping ‣ Critically-Damped Higher-Order Langevin Dynamics" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">10</span></a> is a solution to the recurrence in Equation <a href="#S5.E8" title="In 5.2 From Polynomials to Their Coefficients ‣ 5 Critical Damping ‣ Critically-Damped Higher-Order Langevin Dynamics" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">8</span></a> under the given boundary conditions.</span></p>
</div>
<div id="A4.p3" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A4.p3.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A4.p3.1.1" class="ltx_text">∎</span></p>
</div>
</div>
</section>
